{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T04:02:50.011Z","ordinal":33599,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a1feaf-24d9-7612-a284-664abd64a2c4","turn_id":"01a20691-6d63-7020-b3f3-af8984c725f3","session_id":"01a1feaf-24d9-7612-a284-664abd64a2c4","root_turn_id":"01a20691-6d63-7020-b3f3-af8984c725f3","response_id":"resp_0dca4931a04d8132016b03bade763487d0812af35ed3da5e68","usage":{"input_tokens":434053,"cached_input_tokens":430976,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":363,"reasoning_output_tokens":234,"total_tokens":434416},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":1295745,"cached_input_tokens":1290368,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1160,"reasoning_output_tokens":716,"total_tokens":1296905},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":1198458611,"cached_input_tokens":1193488768,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1044696,"reasoning_output_tokens":283302,"total_tokens":1199503307}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T04:02:50.105Z","ordinal":33600,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1feaf-24d9-7612-a284-664abd64a2c4","turn_id":"01a20691-6d63-7020-b3f3-af8984c725f3","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-5ce5bd2b-7f4b-470e-8d6d-1ac7c45c789c","process_id":"5527","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","head -60 /Users/kingsonwu/.agents/skills/superpowers/test-driven-development/SKILL.md; sed -n '98,147p' frontend/src/features/chat/SearchDialog.test.ts"],"cwd":"file:///Users/kingsonwu/programming/OctopusGarage/mesh-talk","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"head -60 /Users/kingsonwu/.agents/skills/superpowers/test-driven-development/SKILL.md; sed -n '98,147p' frontend/src/features/chat/SearchDialog.test.ts"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"---\nname: test-driven-development\ndescription: Use when implementing any feature or bugfix, before writing implementation code\n---\n\n# Test-Driven Development (TDD)\n\n## Overview\n\nWrite the test first. Watch it fail. Write minimal code to pass.\n\n**Core principle:** If you didn't watch the test fail, you don't know if it tests the right thing.\n\n**Violating the letter of the rules is violating the spirit of the rules.**\n\n## When to Use\n\n**Always:**\n- New features\n- Bug fixes\n- Refactoring\n- Behavior changes\n\n**Exceptions (ask your human partner):**\n- Throwaway prototypes\n- Generated code\n- Configuration files\n\nThinking \"skip TDD just this once\"? Stop. That's rationalization.\n\n## The Iron Law\n\n```\nNO PRODUCTION CODE WITHOUT A FAILING TEST FIRST\n```\n\nWrite code before the test? Delete it. Start over.\n\n**No exceptions:**\n- Don't keep it as \"reference\"\n- Don't \"adapt\" it while writing tests\n- Don't look at it\n- Delete means delete\n\nImplement fresh from tests. Period.\n\n## Red-Green-Refactor\n\n```dot\ndigraph tdd_cycle {\n    rankdir=LR;\n    red [label=\"RED\\nWrite failing test\", shape=box, style=filled, fillcolor=\"#ffcccc\"];\n    verify_red [label=\"Verify fails\\ncorrectly\", shape=diamond];\n    green [label=\"GREEN\\nMinimal code\", shape=box, style=filled, fillcolor=\"#ccffcc\"];\n    verify_green [label=\"Verify passes\\nAll green\", shape=diamond];\n    refactor [label=\"REFACTOR\\nClean up\", shape=box, style=filled, fillcolor=\"#ccccff\"];\n    next [label=\"Next\", shape=ellipse];\n\n    red -> verify_red;\n    verify_red -> green [label=\"yes\"];\n  try {\n    await act(async () => root.render(createElement(SearchDialog)));\n    await act(async () => dialog.onOpenChange?.(true));\n    await act(async () => input.onChange?.({ target: { value: \"term\" } }));\n    await act(async () => vi.advanceTimersByTimeAsync(250));\n    const rows = container.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>(\n      '[data-testid=\"search-result\"]',\n    );\n    expect(rows).toHaveLength(3);\n    await act(async () =>\n      rows[2].dispatchEvent(new MouseEvent(\"mouseover\", { bubbles: true })),\n    );\n    expect(\n      container\n        .querySelector('[role=\"combobox\"]')\n        ?.getAttribute(\"aria-activedescendant\"),\n    ).toBe(\"search-result-2\");\n\n    state.hidden = { bob: {}, carol: {} };\n    await act(async () => root.render(createElement(SearchDialog)));\n    expect(\n      container.querySelectorAll('[data-testid=\"search-result\"]'),\n    ).toHaveLength(1);\n    expect(\n      container\n        .querySelector('[role=\"combobox\"]')\n        ?.getAttribute(\"aria-activedescendant\"),\n    ).toBe(\"search-result-0\");\n    expect(\n      container\n        .querySelector('[data-testid=\"search-result\"]')\n        ?.getAttribute(\"aria-selected\"),\n    ).toBe(\"true\");\n  } finally {\n    await act(async () => root.unmount());\n    vi.useRealTimers();\n    state.hidden = {};\n  }\n});\n\nit(\"opens duplicate results with exact references and refuses unavailable context\", async () => {\n  vi.useFakeTimers();\n  const container = document.createElement(\"div\");\n  const root = createRoot(container);\n  try {\n    api.searchRecent.mockResolvedValueOnce({\n      hits: [\"one\", \"two\"].map((id) => ({\n        is_channel: false,\n        account_id: \"alice\",\n        target: \"alice\",\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":13625}},"started_at_ms":1795406570105,"completed_at_ms":1795406570105}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T04:02:50.621Z","ordinal":33601,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a20692-247d-7ad2-9946-883eb86b1557","call_id":"call_602e636d521a488f883069be5fcdaced","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.8 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"be7a7f\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000013625,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":806,\"output\":\"---\\nname: test-driven-development\\ndescription: Use when implementing any feature or bugfix, before writing implementation code\\n---\\n\\n# Test-Driven Development (TDD)\\n\\n## Overview\\n\\nWrite the test first. Watch it fail. Write minimal code to pass.\\n\\n**Core principle:** If you didn't watch the test fail, you don't know if it tests the right thing.\\n\\n**Violating the letter of the rules is violating the spirit of the rules.**\\n\\n## When to Use\\n\\n**Always:**\\n- New features\\n- Bug fixes\\n- Refactoring\\n- Behavior changes\\n\\n**Exceptions (ask your human partner):**\\n- Throwaway prototypes\\n- Generated code\\n- Configuration files\\n\\nThinking \\\"skip TDD just this once\\\"? Stop. That's rationalization.\\n\\n## The Iron Law\\n\\n```\\nNO PRODUCTION CODE WITHOUT A FAILING TEST FIRST\\n```\\n\\nWrite code before the test? Delete it. Start over.\\n\\n**No exceptions:**\\n- Don't keep it as \\\"reference\\\"\\n- Don't \\\"adapt\\\" it while writing tests\\n- Don't look at it\\n- Delete means delete\\n\\nImplement fresh from tests. Period.\\n\\n## Red-Green-Refactor\\n\\n```dot\\ndigraph tdd_cycle {\\n    rankdir=LR;\\n    red [label=\\\"RED\\\\nWrite failing test\\\", shape=box, style=filled, fillcolor=\\\"#ffcccc\\\"];\\n    verify_red [label=\\\"Verify fails\\\\ncorrectly\\\", shape=diamond];\\n    green [label=\\\"GREEN\\\\nMinimal code\\\", shape=box, style=filled, fillcolor=\\\"#ccffcc\\\"];\\n    verify_green [label=\\\"Verify passes\\\\nAll green\\\", shape=diamond];\\n    refactor [label=\\\"REFACTOR\\\\nClean up\\\", shape=box, style=filled, fillcolor=\\\"#ccccff\\\"];\\n    next [label=\\\"Next\\\", shape=ellipse];\\n\\n    red -> verify_red;\\n    verify_red -> green [label=\\\"yes\\\"];\\n  try {\\n    await act(async () => root.render(createElement(SearchDialog)));\\n    await act(async () => dialog.onOpenChange?.(true));\\n    await act(async () => input.onChange?.({ target: { value: \\\"term\\\" } }));\\n    await act(async () => vi.advanceTimersByTimeAsync(250));\\n    const rows = container.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>(\\n      '[data-testid=\\\"search-result\\\"]',\\n    );\\n    expect(rows).toHaveLength(3);\\n    await act(async () =>\\n      rows[2].dispatchEvent(new MouseEvent(\\\"mouseover\\\", { bubbles: true })),\\n    );\\n    expect(\\n      container\\n        .querySelector('[role=\\\"combobox\\\"]')\\n        ?.getAttribute(\\\"aria-activedescendant\\\"),\\n    ).toBe(\\\"search-result-2\\\");\\n\\n    state.hidden = { bob: {}, carol: {} };\\n    await act(async () => root.render(createElement(SearchDialog)));\\n    expect(\\n      container.querySelectorAll('[data-testid=\\\"search-result\\\"]'),\\n    ).toHaveLength(1);\\n    expect(\\n      container\\n        .querySelector('[role=\\\"combobox\\\"]')\\n        ?.getAttribute(\\\"aria-activedescendant\\\"),\\n    ).toBe(\\\"search-result-0\\\");\\n    expect(\\n      container\\n        .querySelector('[data-testid=\\\"search-result\\\"]')\\n        ?.getAttribute(\\\"aria-selected\\\"),\\n    ).toBe(\\\"true\\\");\\n  } finally {\\n    await act(async () => root.unmount());\\n    vi.useRealTimers();\\n    state.hidden = {};\\n  }\\n});\\n\\nit(\\\"opens duplicate results with exact references and refuses unavailable context\\\", async () => {\\n  vi.useFakeTimers();\\n  const container = document.createElement(\\\"div\\\");\\n  const root = createRoot(container);\\n  try {\\n    api.searchRecent.mockResolvedValueOnce({\\n      hits: [\\\"one\\\", \\\"two\\\"].map((id) => ({\\n        is_channel: false,\\n        account_id: \\\"alice\\\",\\n        target: \\\"alice\\\",\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a20691-6d63-7020-b3f3-af8984c725f3","create_time":1795406570.621322}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":14275,"sampled_through_sequence":14271,"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000,"model_search_state":"unused"}}
