nnounce(&sender, b\"identity\", receiver.local_addr().unwrap())\ncrates/mesh-talk-core/src/discovery/visibility.rs:306:                .send_announce(&sender, b\"public\", receiver.local_addr().unwrap())\ncrates/mesh-talk-core/src/discovery/visibility.rs:315:                .send_announce(&sender, b\"identity\", receiver.local_addr().unwrap())\ncrates/mesh-talk-core/src/discovery/visibility.rs:336:            .send_announce(&sender, b\"identity\", receiver.local_addr().unwrap())\ncrates/mesh-talk-core/src/discovery/visibility.rs:371:                .send_announce(&sender, b\"identity\", receiver.local_addr().unwrap())\ncrates/mesh-talk-core/src/discovery/service.rs:418:                                        visibility.send_announce(&socket, &reply, source).await;\ncrates/mesh-talk-core/src/discovery/service.rs:473:                                let _ = visibility.send_announce(&socket, &bytes, source).await;\ncrates/mesh-talk-core/src/discovery/service.rs:497:                        .send_announce(&socket, &bytes, reply_target)\ncrates/mesh-talk-core/src/discovery/service.rs:578:            let _ = visibility.send_announce(&socket, &bytes, target).await;\ncrates/mesh-talk-core/src/discovery/service.rs:581:        let _ = visibility.send_announce(&socket, &bytes, target).await;\ncrates/mesh-talk-core/src/discovery/service.rs:599:        let _ = visibility.send_announce(&socket, &bytes, target).await;\ncrates/mesh-talk-core/src/discovery/service.rs:827:                visibility.send_announce(socket, bytes, target).await,\ncrates/mesh-talk-core/src/discovery/service.rs:945:            visibility.send_announce(socket, bytes, target).await,\ncrates/mesh-talk-core/src/node/privacy_runtime_tests.rs:3100:            .send_announce(&sender, b\"presence\", receiver.local_addr().unwrap())\n\n## Design and review rules\n\n1. **Trigger work from meaning.** Prefer committed changes, scoped invalidations,\n   user navigation and foreground activation. Schedule the next actual expiry or\n   retry deadline. Empty success is not progress and must not keep a fast retry\n   hot. Coalesce duplicate wakes; retain bounded dirty work while a task is busy.\n   Before adding a subscription or timer, use the [event-driven design guide](event-driven-design.md)\n   to locate the owning event and scheduling mechanisms. Reuse scoped watch\n   signals for projections that can read current state. Use the existing lifecycle owner for deadlines,\n   throttling, retries and periodic repair. Document the trigger, cancellation\n   boundary, missed-signal recovery and the reason for any recurring idle work.\n   Native reception alerts follow the core UI-generation watch and reserve a\n   one-shot delay only when a pending change arrives before the next allowed\n   observation. Durable reception remains independent.\n   Pending work still owns its retry deadline. Suppress unchanged ordinary wakes\n   using scheduling evidence, independently of successful completion; preserve\n   explicit drivers and event-only progress when no timer owns continuation.\n   A retained blocked task is not evidence of progress: keep its recovery fact\n   while backing off, and resume promptly on dependency changes. Local pagination\n   and actual received bytes retain prompt continuation.\n   Reconfirming an already-held relay copy is not new progress. Park unchanged\n   successful reconciliation until sparse repair; keep authenticated recipient\n   delivery and actual custody-loss recovery separate from that scheduling hint.\n## Use on every change\n\n1. **Locate the owner and consumers.** Read the owning implementation, callers,\n   existing tests and relevant guide before adding another helper or state owner.\n   Include callbacks, IPC handlers, retries, startup, shutdown and recovery paths;\n   an import graph alone cannot reveal all consumers.\n2. **State the invariant and select risks.** Describe what must remain true on\n   success, failure, cancellation and replacement. Use the table below to select\n   applicable rules. A small diff can change lock order or lifetime semantics.\n3. **Trace the failure path before editing.** For concurrency work, sketch who\n   owns each lock, permit, task and mutable state; what it waits for; and who\n   releases it. For a reproducible bug, construct a focused failing regression.\n   Record unresolved hypotheses as hypotheses, not confirmed defects.\n4. **Implement at the existing boundary.** Preserve authority, durable acceptance,\n   compatibility and resource budgets. Recheck invariants after moving work\n   outside a guard. Evaluate the proposed fix for new races and deadlocks too.\n5. **Verify the changed boundary and report evidence.** Run affected checks and\n   required boundary scenarios under the testing workflow. Explain results,\n   exclusions and unresolved evidence. Update this guide when the defect exposes\n   a reusable failure pattern; follow the maintenance procedure below.\n\nAccessible message summaries are consumer contracts. When photo, expression or\nfile naming changes, update browser selectors and the owning `prScenarios`\nselection together; retain payload, privacy and receipt assertions instead of\nrestoring implementation-specific names for tests. The inline-media owner uses\n`screenshot-portable.spec.ts` and `automatic-delivery.spec.ts` to cover screenshot\nsending and group custody alongside the presentation scenarios.\n\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":32625}},"started_at_ms":1795407127283,"completed_at_ms":1795407127284}}
