 NET_ADDRESS_INFO, portnumber : *mut u16, prefixlength : *mut u8) -> u32);\n//! LAN peer discovery: nodes broadcast Ed25519-signed [`announce::Announce`]\n//! datagrams carrying their identity keys + TCP port; receivers verify them and\n//! build a roster mapping `user_id` → keys + address. Replaces the legacy\n//! plaintext UDP discovery (which carried no keys).\n\npub mod announce;\npub mod candidates;\n#[cfg(target_os = \"linux\")]\nmod interface_events;\npub mod query;\npub mod roster;\npub(crate) mod scope;\npub mod service;\npub mod visibility;\n\npub use announce::Announce;\nThe desired user experience is that reachable, permitted participants can discover one another and communicate without choosing a global hub. The implementation must still preserve the distinctions between network reachability, device identity, visibility, conversation authority and delivery confirmation.\n\nA client connected to a remote post office can **join that post office's Mesh Talk network**: it can discover eligible registered participants and communicate through the relay. This is application-level participation. It does not install IP routes to every remote machine, forward Ethernet multicast, grant group membership or export all of the client's LAN neighbors.\n\n### Network handoff\n\nDiscovery observes Linux interface identities and addresses on kernel notifications\nand retains a 30-second inventory and multicast join repair. Other platforms and\nfailed Linux subscriptions check every two seconds. An inventory change wakes\nthe existing gated producers. Queue replay and authenticated receipts remain owned by the delivery\nruntime. Network-namespace handoff acceptance and its limits are maintained in\n[routed discovery](routed-network-discovery.md#network-changes-and-recovery).\nPhysical Wi-Fi/hotspot latency remains a separate hardware acceptance boundary.\n\naarch64-apple-darwin\nwasm32-unknown-unknown\nx86_64-apple-darwin\nx86_64-pc-windows-gnu\nx86_64-pc-windows-msvc\nx86_64-unknown-linux-gnu\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a2069c-657a-7d60-9de7-15fae0d142a2","create_time":1795407258.829207}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":14450,"sampled_through_sequence":14447,"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000,"model_search_state":"unused"}}
