           \"periodic_private_probes_reuse_fresh_signed_discovery_but_network_change_forces_noise\",\n658:            \"node::privacy_runtime::tests::discovery_snapshot_\",\n695:            \"name\": \"Local admission backpressure preserves account-sync cursors and verified protocol support, releases bounded workers and retains document pages in their deadline-gated scheduler queue even without a remote continuation; recovery needs no fresh discovery or user wake and cannot spin on coalesced wakes.\",\n727:            \"name\": \"A failed unchanged historical endpoint waits five minutes across background callers; cancellation and local pressure do not learn remote failure. Exact identity/endpoint, privacy/network generations, fresh discovery and successful authentication retain prompt recovery.\",\n731:            \"name\": \"Periodic private probes reuse only sufficiently fresh direct signed discovery for the exact full binding and endpoint; deadline-minus-handshake-budget recovery, forced network/manual probes, authenticated-only lease renewal and fair cancellation ownership remain intact.\",\n735:            \"name\": \"Repeated known routes validate full keys before cloning; discovery snapshots use bounded operation-local full Ed/X/account indexes, preserve peer order and current policy, and expose persistence failure without publishing uncommitted route changes.\",\n/opt/homebrew/bin/x86_64-w64-mingw32-gcc\nreq011-linux-desktop-current-build Up 15 minutes\ntokio-1.52.3\ntokio-1.53.2\ntokio-1.53.3\ntokio-1.54.1\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":10750}},"started_at_ms":1795407296931,"completed_at_ms":1795407296931}}
