erve a participant-consented original registration office across encrypted directory and federation hops without disclosing it by default.\",\n        \"guide\": \"docs/network-design-reference.md#optional-registration-origin-disclosure\",\n        \"invariants\": [\n          {\n            \"name\": \"Both signatures bind the exact participant and office; optional origin never establishes physical location or transport authority\",\n            \"reference\": \"docs/network-design-reference.md#optional-registration-origin-disclosure\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"name\": \"Opt-out serializes with active sends and invalidates prepared work; original 15-second consent leases cannot be renewed by forwarding or presentation tolerance\",\n            \"reference\": \"docs/network-design-reference.md#optional-registration-origin-disclosure\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"name\": \"Legacy discovery and mailbox wire layouts stay compatible and carry no optional origin disclosure\",\n            \"reference\": \"docs/network-design-reference.md#optional-registration-origin-disclosure\"\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      \"escalation\": [\n        \"Run encrypted loopback registration/federation/viewer and opt-out scenarios, host settings/session and presence projection tests, and frontend independent metadata-expiry tests. Physical Windows/macOS office topology still needs native acceptance; loopback does not certify deployment.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"core-authenticated-route-order\",\n      \"paths\": [\n        \"crates/mesh-talk-core/src/node/privacy_runtime.rs\",\n        \"crates/mesh-talk-core/src/node/privacy_runtime_tests.rs\"\n      ],\n      \"rust\": [\n        {\n          \"package\": \"mesh-talk-core\",\n          \"filters\": [\n            \"authenticated_preferred_route_keeps_last_slot_ahead_of_known_stalled_route\",\n            \"fresh_one_off_routes_lead_and_signed_ports_supersede_cached_ports\",\n            \"reachable_route_is_not_blocked_by_stalled_former_lan_handshake\",\n            \"alternate_route_reclaims_idle_sessions_before_waiting_on_stale_route\",\n            \"liveness_dial_deadline_includes_admission_and_releases_policy_writer\",\n            \"liveness_control_dial_deadline_includes_admission_and_releases_policy_writer\",\n            \"liveness_control_dial_cancellation_releases_authentication_and_socket_owners\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ],\n      \"capability\": {\n        \"summary\": \"Keep authenticated working routes ahead of already known supplied endpoints while preserving fresh one-off precedence and signed port replacement.\",\n        \"guide\": \"docs/routed-network-discovery.md#network-changes-and-recovery\",\n        \"invariants\": [\n          {\n            \"name\": \"A known stalled supplied route cannot consume the last outbound slot ahead of an authenticated preferred route; fresh unknown endpoints and signed port replacement retain their existing meaning.\",\n            \"reference\": \"docs/routed-network-discovery.md#network-changes-and-recovery\"\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      \"escalation\": [\n        \"Use the real loopback single-slot stalled-route regression and signed-port/fresh-endpoint tests; physical VM NAT discovery and native delivery remain separate environment acceptance.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\nrustc 1.99.1 (58cf8f9c3 2026-10-13) (Homebrew)\nstable-aarch64-apple-darwin (default)\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":11042}},"started_at_ms":1795407347533,"completed_at_ms":1795407347533}}
