{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T04:16:58.761Z","ordinal":34118,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1feaf-24d9-7612-a284-664abd64a2c4","turn_id":"01a2069c-657a-7d60-9de7-15fae0d142a2","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-c844636d-1e81-443d-9a89-b84275686686","process_id":"62098","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1350,1395p' crates/mesh-talk-core/validation.json\nrg -n 'network changes|interface' docs/routed-network-discovery.md | tail -12\ngit diff --stat -- crates/mesh-talk-core/src/discovery docs/network-design-reference.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/kingsonwu/programming/OctopusGarage/mesh-talk","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"sed -n '1350,1395p' crates/mesh-talk-core/validation.json\nrg -n 'network changes|interface' docs/routed-network-discovery.md | tail -12\ngit diff --stat -- crates/mesh-talk-core/src/discovery docs/network-design-reference.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"      \"escalation\": [\n        \"Validate actual installed desktop and CLI idle behavior separately from unit timing. Require original signed-event offline/reconnect and held-remote progress evidence; pure-helper counters do not establish production-parent scheduling or physical cross-device convergence. The two-parent fixture treats only precommit metadata StaleCursor as pending within its original twenty-second setup/observation deadline; storage, authorization and expected-revision conflicts remain fatal. Preserve the signed announcement, real bidirectional warmup, and unchanged source/scan/distribution counters across the original quiet window.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"core-discovery\",\n      \"paths\": [\"crates/mesh-talk-core/src/discovery/\"],\n      \"rust\": [\n        {\n          \"package\": \"mesh-talk-core\",\n          \"filters\": [\n            \"discovery::\",\n            \"node::runtime::privacy_tests::certified_discovery_requires_a_fresh_reply_despite_cached_peer\",\n            \"node::runtime::privacy_tests::explicit_certified_discovery_retires_ambient_producers_before_first_poll\",\n            \"node::participant_runtime::ambient_retirement_tests::\",\n            \"node::runtime::privacy_tests::pairing_previously_known_foreign_device_survives_both_runtime_restarts\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ],\n      \"escalation\": [\n        \"Discovery fixture completion requires this invocation's nonce and exact endpoint plus an actually accepted device/account binding, not a warm cached row alone. Preserve its original deadline and probe cadence/count. Run real warm-cache stopped-target/restart controls and UDP witness acceptance/rejection, bound, instance isolation, disabled formatting and joined listener retirement. Explicit-endpoint fixtures retire three named ambient producers before first poll through their participant owner, retaining real listener/public-policy/certificates/TCP/delivery. Verify normal-startup rejection, zero first polls, all actual joins and cleanup-before-failure reporting; production still launches all four tasks. Test-only traces remain opt-in; fixture isolation does not resolve production socket pressure or establish an unobserved historical cause. See docs/ci-maintenance.md.\",\n        \"Public core API, crypto, wire or persisted storage changes require affected consumer review and focused loopback/restart or compatibility evidence; development library selectors do not certify integration or native acceptance.\",\n        \"Pinned gateway queries must recover when another loopback client consumes the existing per-source UDP reply quota. Preserve the absolute four-second deadline, at most four datagrams, exact endpoint and signed pinned-identity validation, and cancellation ownership. Run the real responder quota regression and existing gateway lifecycle/security tests; repeat bridge_cross_lan and channel_peer_recovery against the production CLI.\"\n      ],\n      \"capability\": {\n        \"summary\": \"Authenticate bounded signed discovery proofs while preserving current presence, account and transport authority.\",\n        \"guide\": \"docs/network-design-reference.md#person-presence-contract\",\n        \"invariants\": [\n          {\n            \"name\": \"Linux link and address notifications invalidate the authoritative interface snapshot. Subscription failure retains the two-second polling fallback, receive overflow reconciles immediately, and the 30-second repair preserves multicast membership and missed-signal recovery.\",\n            \"reference\": \"docs/routed-network-discovery.md#network-changes-and-recovery\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"name\": \"Exact complete successful announcement proofs, including both signatures, may reuse intrinsic verification in a process-local 128-entry, 256-KiB metadata owner. Invalid results are not retained; changed fields reverify. Oversized inputs, contention, poison and eviction preserve original verification semantics without waiting or crypto under a guard. Current presence, account binding, revocation, visibility, discovery challenges and Noise authorization remain fresh; wire, SDK and storage formats are unchanged. Relayed name-only updates publish the existing roster observation while same-name route renewals remain quiet; descriptive-name invalidation grants no presence or account authority.\",\n            \"reference\": \"docs/ai-coding-reliability.md#r08-durable-state-and-failure-semantics\"\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      \"consumers\": [\"core-node\", \"core-postoffice\", \"core-transport\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"core-dm\",\n      \"paths\": [\"crates/mesh-talk-core/src/dm.rs\"],\n      \"rust\": [\n        {\n          \"package\": \"mesh-talk-core\",\n22:Both feed the same core `CandidateSource` interface. Collection runs concurrently\n76:cached ports. IPv4/IPv6 support follows available sockets and interface scope.\n80:Desktop, CLI and post-office discovery observe non-loopback interface names,\n81:addresses and interface indexes. Linux reconciles on link or address notifications.\n90:Fresh signed announcements supply current TCP endpoints. Changed local interfaces\n106:`scripts/e2e-network-handoff.py` moves disposable Linux container interfaces between\n crates/mesh-talk-core/src/discovery/mod.rs     |  5 ++\n crates/mesh-talk-core/src/discovery/service.rs | 84 ++++++++++++++++++++++++--\n docs/network-design-reference.md               | 19 ++++--\n 3 files changed, 99 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":11084}},"started_at_ms":1795407418761,"completed_at_ms":1795407418761}}
