{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T04:17:06.903Z","ordinal":34124,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0dca4931a04d8132016b03be3d933087d0a511579bbf532c9d","status":"completed","call_id":"call_dfef7136f90541ec829ce2bd061543d9","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:`sed -n '78,90p' docs/routed-network-discovery.md\npython3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('crates/mesh-talk-core/validation.json');s=p.read_text();s=s.replace('Linux link and address notifications invalidate the authoritative interface snapshot. Subscription failure retains the two-second polling fallback, receive overflow reconciles immediately, and the 30-second repair preserves multicast membership and missed-signal recovery.', 'Linux and Windows link and address notifications invalidate the authoritative interface snapshot. Subscription failure retains the two-second polling fallback, Linux receive overflow reconciles immediately, and the 30-second repair preserves multicast membership and missed-signal recovery. Windows callbacks coalesce into one pending wake and retire with the discovery task.');p.write_text(s)\np=Path('docs/routed-network-discovery.md');s=p.read_text();s=s.replace('Linux reconciles on link or address notifications.', 'Linux and Windows reconcile on link or address notifications.').replace('Other platforms and failed Linux subscriptions', 'Other platforms and failed subscriptions');p.write_text(s)\nPY\nmake standards-check >tmp/req-011/windows-interface-standards.log 2>&1\ngit diff --check`,yield_time_ms:1000}))\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a2069c-657a-7d60-9de7-15fae0d142a2","create_time":1795407421.5787244}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":14499,"sampled_through_sequence":14497,"client_authored":false,"model_search_state":"unused"}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T04:17:06.943Z","ordinal":34125,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a1feaf-24d9-7612-a284-664abd64a2c4","turn_id":"01a2069c-657a-7d60-9de7-15fae0d142a2","session_id":"01a1feaf-24d9-7612-a284-664abd64a2c4","root_turn_id":"01a2069c-657a-7d60-9de7-15fae0d142a2","response_id":"resp_0dca4931a04d8132016b03be3bc5d887d08aa3fe3cfed1f4bd","usage":{"input_tokens":102535,"cached_input_tokens":101248,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":287,"reasoning_output_tokens":11,"total_tokens":102822},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":2048490,"cached_input_tokens":2033024,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":4640,"reasoning_output_tokens":250,"total_tokens":2053130},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":1213476348,"cached_input_tokens":1208394112,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1063835,"reasoning_output_tokens":285462,"total_tokens":1214540183}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T04:17:08.131Z","ordinal":34126,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a2069f-3a23-7033-b9ee-eb0fd82ebc59","call_id":"call_dfef7136f90541ec829ce2bd061543d9","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"183d85\",\"wall_time_seconds\":1.00216225,\"session_id\":81025,\"original_token_count\":203,\"output\":\"## Network changes and recovery\\n\\nDesktop, CLI and post-office discovery observe non-loopback interface names,\\naddresses and interface indexes. Linux reconciles on link or address notifications.\\nOther platforms, or Linux when subscription fails, check every two seconds. A changed inventory\\nrejoins LAN multicast and wakes the existing announce/scan producers; a desktop's\\nshared trigger also refreshes routed candidates. Inventory ordering and duplicates\\ndo not create changes, and an enumeration failure retains the last observation.\\nThe 30-second periodic multicast join remains a retry fallback and also repairs\\nmissed Linux notifications. Every advertisement\\nand routed probe still passes the current visibility/scope gates.\\n\\nFresh signed announcements supply current TCP endpoints. Changed local interfaces\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a2069c-657a-7d60-9de7-15fae0d142a2","create_time":1795407428.13144}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":14500,"sampled_through_sequence":14497,"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000,"model_search_state":"unused"}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T04:17:08.132Z","ordinal":34127,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"token_count","info":{"total_token_usage":{"input_tokens":1209427525,"cached_input_tokens":1204349184,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1041885,"reasoning_output_tokens":285462,"total_tokens":1210469410},"last_token_usage":{"input_tokens":102535,"cached_input_tokens":101248,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":287,"reasoning_output_tokens":11,"total_tokens":102822},"last_usage_includes_reasoning":true,"model_context_window":475000},"rate_limits":{"limit_id":"codex","limit_name":null,"primary":{"used_percent":48.0,"window_minutes":10080,"resets_at":1795755493},"secondary":null,"credits":{"has_credits":true,"unlimited":false,"balance":"19951.9885315000"},"individual_limit":null,"spend_control_reached":null,"plan_type":null,"rate_limit_reached_type":null}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T04:17:09.762Z","ordinal":34128,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1feaf-24d9-7612-a284-664abd64a2c4","turn_id":"01a2069c-657a-7d60-9de7-15fae0d142a2","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-ca4981a3-1b8c-4eac-9b83-2f8540323d33","process_id":"81025","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '78,90p' docs/routed-network-discovery.md\npython3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('crates/mesh-talk-core/validation.json');s=p.read_text();s=s.replace('Linux link and address notifications invalidate the authoritative interface snapshot. Subscription failure retains the two-second polling fallback, receive overflow reconciles immediately, and the 30-second repair preserves multicast membership and missed-signal recovery.', 'Linux and Windows link and address notifications invalidate the authoritative interface snapshot. Subscription failure retains the two-second polling fallback, Linux receive overflow reconciles immediately, and the 30-second repair preserves multicast membership and missed-signal recovery. Windows callbacks coalesce into one pending wake and retire with the discovery task.');p.write_text(s)\np=Path('docs/routed-network-discovery.md');s=p.read_text();s=s.replace('Linux reconciles on link or address notifications.', 'Linux and Windows reconcile on link or address notifications.').replace('Other platforms and failed Linux subscriptions', 'Other platforms and failed subscriptions');p.write_text(s)\nPY\nmake standards-check >tmp/req-011/windows-interface-standards.log 2>&1\ngit diff --check"],"cwd":"file:///Users/kingsonwu/programming/OctopusGarage/mesh-talk","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"sed -n '78,90p' docs/routed-network-discovery.md\npython3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('crates/mesh-talk-core/validation.json');s=p.read_text();s=s.replace('Linux link and address notifications invalidate the authoritative interface snapshot. Subscription failure retains the two-second polling fallback, receive overflow reconciles immediately, and the 30-second repair preserves multicast membership and missed-signal recovery.', 'Linux and Windows link and address notifications invalidate the authoritative interface snapshot. Subscription failure retains the two-second polling fallback, Linux receive overflow reconciles immediately, and the 30-second repair preserves multicast membership and missed-signal recovery. Windows callbacks coalesce into one pending wake and retire with the discovery task.');p.write_text(s)\np=Path('docs/routed-network-discovery.md');s=p.read_text();s=s.replace('Linux reconciles on link or address notifications.', 'Linux and Windows reconcile on link or address notifications.').replace('Other platforms and failed Linux subscriptions', 'Other platforms and failed subscriptions');p.write_text(s)\nPY\nmake standards-check >tmp/req-011/windows-interface-standards.log 2>&1\ngit diff --check"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"## Network changes and recovery\n\nDesktop, CLI and post-office discovery observe non-loopback interface names,\naddresses and interface indexes. Linux reconciles on link or address notifications.\nOther platforms, or Linux when subscription fails, check every two seconds. A changed inventory\nrejoins LAN multicast and wakes the existing announce/scan producers; a desktop's\nshared trigger also refreshes routed candidates. Inventory ordering and duplicates\ndo not create changes, and an enumeration failure retains the last observation.\nThe 30-second periodic multicast join remains a retry fallback and also repairs\nmissed Linux notifications. Every advertisement\nand routed probe still passes the current visibility/scope gates.\n\nFresh signed announcements supply current TCP endpoints. Changed local interfaces\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":2,"nanos":635957209}},"started_at_ms":1795407427126,"completed_at_ms":1795407429762}}
