nvironment for production...\ntransforming...\n✓ 2950 modules transformed.\n4.2G\t/Users/kingsonwu/programming/OctopusGarage/mesh-talk/tmp/req-011/linux-exact-interface-mailbox.YVKhWNWu/target\n505M\t/Users/kingsonwu/programming/OctopusGarage/mesh-talk/tmp/req-011/linux-exact-interface-mailbox.YVKhWNWu/cargo-registry\n# Project-wide resource limits to keep cargo from saturating the CPU.\n#\n# Rationale: cargo sizes both compilation and test parallelism to the number of\n# CPU cores by default, which pins all cores. (Test builds use cheap KDF params via\n# cfg(test)/the fast-test-kdf feature, so the suite is no longer KDF-bound — but a\n# full parallel compile can still saturate a small machine.) These caps apply to\n# EVERY cargo invocation in this tree (CI, contributors, and AI sessions) automatically.\n#\n# Tuned for an 8-core machine at a \"gentle\" ~half-cores level. Adjust the two\n# numbers if you change machines.\n\n[build]\n# Cap parallel compilation units (codegen jobs). ~half of logical cores.\njobs = 4\n\n[env]\n# Cap libtest's parallel test threads so the suite doesn't pin every core at once.\n# Honored by the test harness produced by `cargo test`.\nRUST_TEST_THREADS = \"4\"\n[validation:rust-focused] running for 300s; log /Users/kingsonwu/programming/OctopusGarage/mesh-talk/target/validation/logs/rust-focused-1795409023938-34f49f7b-bad0-48a4-99f7-822bec5d366b.log\n[validation:rust-focused] running for 330s; log /Users/kingsonwu/programming/OctopusGarage/mesh-talk/target/validation/logs/rust-focused-1795409023938-34f49f7b-bad0-48a4-99f7-822bec5d366b.log\n53712       04:47 257.8 2053360 rustc\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":711872875}},"started_at_ms":1795409377250,"completed_at_ms":1795409377963}}
