{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T04:52:50.728Z","ordinal":35701,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1feaf-24d9-7612-a284-664abd64a2c4","turn_id":"01a206bf-0e7f-7bb0-a92c-d6215ac1eb31","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-fd64ef80-b64c-4910-bd9e-1c0d06fa88f7","process_id":"73188","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '267,294p;330,350p' docs/performance-requirements.md\nrg -n 'renderer|projection' docs/ai-coding-reliability.md | head -27\nrg -n 'unchanged|delivery' frontend/validation.json | grep -i 'projection' | head -9"],"cwd":"file:///Users/kingsonwu/programming/OctopusGarage/mesh-talk","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'renderer|projection' docs/ai-coding-reliability.md","query":"renderer|projection","path":"ai-coding-reliability.md"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'unchanged|delivery' frontend/validation.json","query":"unchanged|delivery","path":"validation.json"},{"type":"search","cmd":"grep -i projection","query":"projection","path":null}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"   Apply already-authoritative metadata exclusions before body reads, including\n   inventory rows that a physical local group would later discard.\n\n4. **Bound every retained layer.** Budget bytes/pixels as well as entry count,\n   concurrency and queues. Virtualized DOM is not a bounded data store. Keep a\n   small active window; evict inactive payloads and load originals only on demand.\n   Closed feature imports must not eagerly load their data through another caller;\n   defer the producer as well as its component, with scoped cancellation and retry.\n   Library catalogs and background registration receipts must not retain image\n   URLs or archives. Scope point reads to content revisions, bound concurrent\n   hydration and release inactive payloads; readiness belongs to the selected asset.\n   A bounded native cache does not justify eagerly filling it from an entire\n   library. Query existing pending metadata first, hydrate only matching assets\n   and permit re-demand after eviction. Keep continuation through filtered pages;\n   a row limit alone does not bound nested per-row history traversal.\n   Bound negative caches as well as successful results; eviction permits a later\n   retry instead of retaining every failed identifier until logout.\n   For fully version-qualified derived plans, elapsed idle time alone must not\n   force durable cleanup/rebuild. Bound retained resources by entries and bytes;\n   invalidate on authoritative change, capacity pressure or owner retirement.\n   Time-based credentials, delivery deadlines and network leases remain subject\n   to their own current expiry checks.\n   Compressed file size is not decoded image memory. Avoid keeping archives,\n   base64 strings, Blobs and decoded originals together without a measured need.\n   Reuse expensive unchanged presentation work with bounded semantic keys. Locale\n   and fresh local calendar fields must still qualify date/time results; a cached\n   formatter's original timezone must not pin later output. Cache display strings\n   without retaining message identity or adding another timer.\n   and recovery rule; warn before configured capacity is exhausted. Reuse freed\n   storage and batch compaction instead of rewriting the database after each delete.\n   Evicting a cache must not resurrect deleted messages or lose\n   unread/receipt evidence. Compact tombstones only when a durable floor/epoch or\n   equivalent protocol proof prevents old replicas from reintroducing data.\n7. **Make inactivity and retirement explicit.** Distinguish visible, hidden, call\n   and stopped states. Release unused media and subscriptions. Prove reception,\n   persistence and notifications survive before suspending a page. Actual work\n   retains its permit until completion; stale owners cannot publish late results.\n   Keep indefinite idle states such as discovery without peers visually static.\n   Verify that they do not schedule continuous animation frames or compositor\n   work. Use the [presence browser scenario](../frontend/e2e/person-presence.spec.ts)\n   and native renderer sampling when the state is shown by a desktop WebView.\n\n## Evidence and maintenance\n\nBefore optimizing, identify the owner and capture the offending operation count\nor allocation/CPU/write trace. Add a regression that fails on that mechanism,\nthen validate empty/no-change, growth, failure/retry, cancellation and recovery.\nCompare the same device/build/runtime/profile; include whole-family resource\nmeasurements and a correctness witness. SQL affected-row counts do not measure\n92:Account archive snapshots, history projections and delivery recovery share the\n389:settings projection/restart scenario exercises this boundary with its old weak\n643:A producer revision gate must precede expensive routing filters and projection\n777:Observing a completed projection must not manufacture and immediately retire\n1162:the canonical reader reports a typed stale projection, preserve its existing\n1231:enumeration of display projections. A ready history observation is not a lease\n1232:on subsequent projection readiness, and a generic mutation retry can repeat work\n1234:checks a real pending archived projection, unrelated DM/unknown targets,\n1236:Do not attach unrelated global projection work to a narrow mutation. Text\n1275:not restore mutation authority. A bounded projection may omit existing data;\n1314:first retained alias. The native canonical history projection owns both known\n1325:Optional ingress projection must do no writes when there is no captured source.\n1597:Filter impossible candidates before canonical history or protection projection;\n1670:Trace every consumer of a scheduling projection: relay-control retries, file\n1672:share canonical endpoint semantics. Equal projections preserve owners, completion\n1732:and [pending file projection](../crates/mesh-talk-core/src/node/filebook/indexed.rs)\n1899:metadata/projection pairs under the exact verified own-head hash, with a\n1904:Recall or expiring File inputs retain live projection. Both absolute and first-seen\n2317:projection after retiring its continuously appending peers. Its projection read\n2342:for its later projection; retain exact private-receipt evidence before release.\n2405:text, sticker and file-card Awaiting/explicit projection separately; keep the\n2516:projection between polls. The existing `ready_history` owner in\n2519:authorization controls remain fatal. Indexed queries on an acquired projection\n2561:witnesses its real explicit negotiation and durable projection. It commits its\n2568:retains authenticated public recall and reaction projection even when its\n2592:that the independent plaintext projection is visible. Observe that projection\n683:            \"name\": \"Missing or aged scheduling details do not establish recipient presence, failure, custody or delivery. Independent text, sticker and file-card browser scenarios require Awaiting before one explicit authoritative mock projection; the file scenario retains disclosure, keyboard and offer-receipt assertions without combining three send journeys inside one functional case budget.\",\n2534:            \"name\": \"Receipt persistence coalesces within a fixed 100 ms window and flushes before restoration and owner retirement; unchanged conversations retain immutable projections and existing unread/alias bounds.\",\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":10459}},"started_at_ms":1795409570727,"completed_at_ms":1795409570728}}
