{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T05:05:01.950Z","ordinal":36158,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1feaf-24d9-7612-a284-664abd64a2c4","turn_id":"01a206ca-8bd3-7e61-8a39-400f1dbe0d63","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-fa9913c0-6a63-4ee8-8dd4-d52414acab52","process_id":"40833","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '92,145p' docs/event-driven-design.md\nrg -n '^#{1,3} ' docs/post-office-federation.md | head -24\nps -axo pid,ppid,command | rg 'req011-linux-desktop-rerender|native-lock-policy-tests|parallel-policy|parallel-comparison|mac-interface-integrated-tests' | cut -c1-185\ntail -8 tmp/req-011/native-lock-policy-tests.log 2>/dev/null"],"cwd":"file:///Users/kingsonwu/programming/OctopusGarage/mesh-talk","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"sed -n '92,145p' docs/event-driven-design.md\nrg -n '^#{1,3} ' docs/post-office-federation.md | head -24\nps -axo pid,ppid,command | rg 'req011-linux-desktop-rerender|native-lock-policy-tests|parallel-policy|parallel-comparison|mac-interface-integrated-tests' | cut -c1-185\ntail -8 tmp/req-011/native-lock-policy-tests.log 2>/dev/null"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"  return () => {\n    active = false;\n    unsubscribe();\n  };\n}, [owner, requestDocumentRefresh]);\n```\n\nHere `requestDocumentRefresh` represents the feature's existing refresh\noperation. The callback guard controls entry. The operation itself must check\nowner and lifetime again before applying an asynchronous result.\n\nFor a new event family, record its owner, producer, source identifier, scope,\ncommit timing, authorized consumers, initial read and recovery path. Record\nwhether it may coalesce, duplicate, reorder, drop or replay. Also record its\ncapacity, cancellation boundary and the focused regression for these rules.\n\n## Schedule work by purpose\n\nSee [Scheduled work and recovery](scheduled-work.md) for existing components,\nregistration contracts and verification.\n\n| Purpose | Reuse policy |\n| --- | --- |\n| Absolute expiry or lease | Reuse the owning expiry path, such as [chat expiry](../frontend/src/store/chatExpiry.ts). Schedule the nearest deadline and recompute after resume. Preserve persisted expiry and authority across restart. |\n| Coalesce a burst | Store the pending revision or dirty bit. Schedule at most one trailing delay or animation frame as appropriate. Define whether sustained input may defer the work and bound that delay. |\n| Retry transient failure | Keep the existing retry/backoff owner and classify failures that may retry. Allow a meaningful dependency change to wake blocked work when its contract permits it. Preserve concurrency and due-work limits. |\n| Repair missed invalidation | Reconcile through the owner's snapshot or cursor on startup, reconnect or foreground. Use a sparse fallback where delivery can be absent or incomplete. Measure necessity before changing it. |\n| Limit an active operation | Use the operation's timeout and cancellation owner. A caller giving up does not free a native concurrency slot until the operation actually retires. See [serial refresh](../frontend/src/features/chat/useSerialPoll.ts). |\n| Drive live protocol or presentation | Heartbeats, active ringtone cadence and frame-bound gestures have their own lifetimes. Stop their scheduling when the owning session or interaction ends. |\n\nReuse policy and lifecycle ownership within each runtime. Introduce a shared\nhelper once callers demonstrate the same scheduling semantics and cancellation\nrequirements. Core, desktop Host and WebView each keep their executor and\nresource ownership.\n\n## Review an existing polling path\n\nDocument its trigger, cadence, actual work, foreground and background scope,\nrecovery guarantee, and cancellation path. Check whether a reliable producer\nalready signals the relevant state and whether the listener can reconstruct\ncurrent state after loss. Test idle, a burst, a change during an in-flight read,\nlistener retirement, runtime replacement, and missed or duplicate notification\nas applicable. Keep retry, expiry, heartbeat and recovery controls specific to\nthe affected contract.\n\nStart with redundant observation work such as a timer that only checks an\nexisting watch. Consolidate lifecycle listeners when their consumers genuinely\nshare a policy. Measure both normal foreground operation and return to idle,\nincluding wakeups, CPU, latency, and bounded pending work. Keep OS-level\nmeasurements separate from paused-clock scheduling tests.\n\nFor the next app-wide review, inspect these candidates in order of how clearly\ntheir replacements can preserve behavior:\n\n1:# Equal post-office federation\n14:## Responsibilities and boundaries\n27:## Automatic membership in an approved network\n119:## One shared public configuration\n145:# Full device fingerprint followed by numeric IP and discovery UDP port.\n161:## Boot services\n178:## Enrollment, revocation and rotation\n201:## Capacity and compatibility\n236:## Indexed relay runtime and resource bounds\n300:### Opt-in ingestion observation\n318:### Unchanged federation refreshes\n356:## Failure behavior and verification\n 8097 86345 docker run --rm --name req011-linux-desktop-rerender-build --cpus 3 -m 8g -v /Users/kingsonwu/programming/OctopusGarage/mesh-talk/tmp/req-011/linux-desktop-rerender.k9COCpq4\n13734  8097 /Applications/Docker.app/Contents/Resources/bin/com.docker.cli run --rm --name req011-linux-desktop-rerender-build --cpus 3 -m 8g -v /Users/kingsonwu/programming/OctopusGara\n24064 86345 /bin/zsh -c sed -n '92,145p' docs/event-driven-design.md\\012rg -n '^#{1,3} ' docs/post-office-federation.md | head -24\\012ps -axo pid,ppid,command | rg 'req011-linux-desktop\n24076 24064 rg req011-linux-desktop-rerender|native-lock-policy-tests|parallel-policy|parallel-comparison|mac-interface-integrated-tests\n26981 86345 /bin/zsh -c set -e\\012out=$(cat tmp/req-011/linux-desktop-rerender-path)\\012old=$(cat tmp/req-011/linux-accelerated-path)\\012v=$(cat \"$old/source-volume\")\\012r=$(realpath \"$\n37769 86345 /bin/zsh -c set -e\\012while kill -0 93190 2>/dev/null; do sleep 8; done\\012make test-focused TEST_PACKAGE=mesh-talk TEST_FILTER=app_lock:: >tmp/req-011/native-lock-policy-te\n54028 86345 /bin/zsh -c python3 - <<'PY'\\012from pathlib import Path\\012for name in ['docs/network-design-reference.md', 'docs/routed-network-discovery.md', 'crates/mesh-talk-core/valid\n75608 86345 /bin/zsh -c set -e\\012m=$(cat tmp/req-011/native-proof-gated-path)\\012h=\"$m/startup-harness\"\\012cp \"$h/measure-warm-native.py\" \"$h/measure-warm-native-footprint.py\"\\012pytho\n[validation:rust-focused] started after 0s queue; log /Users/kingsonwu/programming/OctopusGarage/mesh-talk/target/validation/logs/rust-focused-1795410205174-5dd46e23-f0ba-4ebe-b473-6a8d1b7de77e.log\n   Compiling mesh-talk-core v0.4.6 (/Users/kingsonwu/programming/OctopusGarage/mesh-talk/crates/mesh-talk-core)\n   Compiling mesh-talk-integrations v0.4.6 (/Users/kingsonwu/programming/OctopusGarage/mesh-talk/crates/mesh-talk-integrations)\n[validation:rust-focused] running for 30s; log /Users/kingsonwu/programming/OctopusGarage/mesh-talk/target/validation/logs/rust-focused-1795410205174-5dd46e23-f0ba-4ebe-b473-6a8d1b7de77e.log\n[validation:rust-focused] running for 60s; log /Users/kingsonwu/programming/OctopusGarage/mesh-talk/target/validation/logs/rust-focused-1795410205174-5dd46e23-f0ba-4ebe-b473-6a8d1b7de77e.log\n[validation:rust-focused] running for 90s; log /Users/kingsonwu/programming/OctopusGarage/mesh-talk/target/validation/logs/rust-focused-1795410205174-5dd46e23-f0ba-4ebe-b473-6a8d1b7de77e.log\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":6583625}},"started_at_ms":1795410301943,"completed_at_ms":1795410301950}}
