{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T05:05:18.562Z","ordinal":36170,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1feaf-24d9-7612-a284-664abd64a2c4","turn_id":"01a206ca-8bd3-7e61-8a39-400f1dbe0d63","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-bcfc9fea-2598-4e23-b1fe-ebc5a856b16b","process_id":"20845","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","kill -TERM 26981 75608\ndocker stop --time 5 req011-linux-desktop-rerender-build\nsed -n '233,249p' docs/post-office-federation.md\nsed -n '1,27p' docs/scheduled-work.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/kingsonwu/programming/OctopusGarage/mesh-talk","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"kill -TERM 26981 75608\ndocker stop --time 5 req011-linux-desktop-rerender-build\nsed -n '233,249p' docs/post-office-federation.md\nsed -n '1,27p' docs/scheduled-work.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"req011-linux-desktop-rerender-build\nlarge graphs of slow or unreachable peers can still lengthen a reconciliation\nround.\n\n## Indexed relay runtime and resource bounds\n\nThe dedicated CLI serves plain mailboxes, named bridges/gateways, pinned\nfederation and approved-network federation through one encrypted indexed store\nand shared endpoint. Normal reopen does not load retained ciphertext bodies or\nall historical IDs. Legacy import is a separate authenticated migration; the\nparticipant runtime and collecting SDK APIs keep their separate storage behavior.\n\nOne endpoint shares four nonwaiting Have reservations, each with 32 MiB logical\naccounting, including vector-to-set overlap and retained use. Saturation returns\nlocal retryable overload rather than waiting with partial reservations. The\n128 MiB aggregate is a Have accounting budget, not a measured process RSS cap.\nFederation staging admits at most 512 outstanding sessions, 262,144 entries and\n64 MiB accounted storage across both remote inventory and selected local digests;\n# Scheduled work and recovery\n\nUse this guide when a feature needs work to run at a deadline, retry after a\nfailure, or reconcile after missing an event. The [event-driven design\nguide](event-driven-design.md) owns event semantics and subscription rules.\nThe [performance guide](performance-requirements.md) owns resource budgets.\n\n## Choose an existing owner\n\n| Work | Existing entry point or reference | When to use it |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Refresh visible data from a scoped event | [useSerialPoll](../frontend/src/features/chat/useSerialPoll.ts) | A renderer view needs an initial read, event-driven refresh, a foreground catch-up and a visible fallback. The hook serializes actual reads, retains one pending invalidation and stops its timer while hidden. Select a supported invalidation scope and provide the feature's snapshot read. |\n| Recheck an external setting on activation | [startRecoveryRefresh](../frontend/src/lib/recoveryRefresh.ts) | A renderer owner needs a coalesced foreground check. Set the interval to null for activation-only recovery, as used for native notification permission. |\n| Enforce a UI read deadline | [readWithDeadline](../frontend/src/lib/readDeadline.ts) | The WebView needs to stop waiting for a read. Its shared admission limit stays occupied until the real native operation settles. Mutations and native cancellation have separate owners. |\n| Retire expiring UI state | [Chat expiry](../frontend/src/store/chatExpiry.ts) and [contact expiry](../frontend/src/store/rosterRefresh.ts) | Data already supplies an expiry timestamp. Update the existing feature state so its owner can rearm the nearest deadline. The Host remains authoritative for business expiry. |\n| Observe Host work after a runtime is installed | [NodeRuntime host-task registration](../crates/mesh-talk-core/src/node/runtime.rs) | The task belongs to an authenticated runtime. Register it with the runtime so retirement closes admission and joins owned work. Use graceful registration for adapters that need asynchronous cleanup. |\n| Rate-limit a pending Host observation | [Native reception alerts](../src-tauri/src/reception_host.rs) | An existing watch is reliable. Await the watch and arm one delay only if a pending observation arrives before its next eligible time. |\n| Refresh from a native event with a sparse safety check | [Network cost observer](../src-tauri/src/network_cost/mod.rs) | Native inputs may be missed or unavailable. The Linux and Windows adapter serializes the initial query, change-triggered queries and five-minute repair. macOS uses its native callback path. |\n| Project an account nickname into desktop credentials | [Account profile commit watch](../crates/mesh-talk-core/src/node/account_profile_data/indexed.rs) and [Host runtime projection](../src-tauri/src/runtime_bootstrap.rs) | The signed own-account profile is authoritative. Reconcile once on installation and wake on committed changes. Failed reads or credential writes retry after 500 ms. A five-minute repair deadline covers missed work. |\n| Reconcile private account access across linked devices | [Account access worker](../crates/mesh-talk-core/src/node/account_access.rs) and [linked-device store](../crates/mesh-talk-core/src/node/account_devices.rs) | Subscribe before the initial scan. Park without a timer when no certified sibling has an observed route. A committed certificate or a roster change can add eligible work. While a route exists, retain the worker's existing policy reconciliation and retry fences. |\n| Schedule retries for delivery | [Core delivery retry owner](../crates/mesh-talk-core/src/node/delivery_retry.rs) and [file delivery scheduler](../crates/mesh-talk-core/src/node/delivery_runtime.rs) | Work already belongs to delivery. Keep its destination keys, retry eligibility, worker limits and durable progress with that owner. After an empty successful scan with no admitted file/control work and no verified or bridged pull demand, rely on accepted-work and route signals with a five-minute repair deadline. Errors retain the normal recovery pace. |\n| Combine multiple deadlines with changes | [Core profile publication loop](../crates/mesh-talk-core/src/node/runtime.rs) | A runtime owner already has change subscriptions, pending operations and semantic deadlines. Await the nearest known deadline alongside those signals. |\n\nReuse the entry point that already owns the business work. Reference examples\nshow the scheduling pattern to follow when a different lifecycle or authority\nrequires its own owner.\n\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":7,"nanos":937544500}},"started_at_ms":1795410310605,"completed_at_ms":1795410318562}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T05:05:18.578Z","ordinal":36171,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1feaf-24d9-7612-a284-664abd64a2c4","turn_id":"01a206bc-a912-7213-a74f-ff0796798220","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-438c913e-7c84-4050-92fc-a9b93d3a9815","process_id":"18984","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","set -e\nset -o pipefail\nold=$(cat tmp/req-011/linux-desktop-current-path)\ncache=$(cat tmp/req-011/linux-exact-interface-mailbox-path)\nout=$(mktemp -d \"$PWD/tmp/req-011/linux-desktop-rerender.XXXXXXXX\")\nprintf '%s\\n' \"$out\" >tmp/req-011/linux-desktop-rerender-path\nmkdir \"$out/source\"\ngit rev-parse HEAD >\"$out/source-sha\"\ngit diff --binary | shasum -a 256 >\"$out/diff-sha256\"\ngit ls-files -z --cached --others --exclude-standard | COPYFILE_DISABLE=1 tar -cf - --null -T - | tar -xf - -C \"$out/source\"\ncmp \"$old/source/frontend/package-lock.json\" \"$out/source/frontend/package-lock.json\"\ncp -cR \"$old/source/frontend/node_modules\" \"$out/source/frontend/\"\nmkdir -p \"$out/source/src-tauri/src/bin\"\ncp \"$old/source/src-tauri/src/bin/req011-driverless-loaded.rs\" \"$out/source/src-tauri/src/bin/\"\ncp \"$old\"/{run-isolated-x11.sh,run-native.sh,run-with-window-manager.sh,sample-family.py,summarize-native.py,compare-native-memory.py,reference-metadata.json} \"$out/\"\nshasum -a 256 \"$out/source/src-tauri/src/bin/req011-driverless-loaded.rs\" >\"$out/fixture-source.sha256\"\nwhile kill -0 93190 2>/dev/null; do sleep 8; done\ndocker run --rm --name req011-linux-desktop-rerender-build --cpus 3 -m 8g \\\n  -v \"$out/source:/candidate\" -v \"$cache/target:/cargo-target\" \\\n  -v \"$cache/cargo-registry:/usr/local/cargo/registry\" -v \"$out:/evidence\" \\\n  -e CARGO_TARGET_DIR=/cargo-target -w /candidate mesh-talk-req011-native-wm:local bash -ceu '\n    (cd frontend && npm run build)\n    cargo build --locked --release -j 2 -p mesh-talk --bin req011-driverless-loaded\n    cp /cargo-target/release/req011-driverless-loaded /evidence/\n    cd /evidence\n    sha256sum req011-driverless-loaded >native-binary.sha256\n  ' >\"$out/native-build.log\" 2>&1"],"cwd":"file:///Users/kingsonwu/programming/OctopusGarage/mesh-talk","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"set -e\nset -o pipefail\nold=$(cat tmp/req-011/linux-desktop-current-path)\ncache=$(cat tmp/req-011/linux-exact-interface-mailbox-path)\nout=$(mktemp -d \"$PWD/tmp/req-011/linux-desktop-rerender.XXXXXXXX\")\nprintf '%s\\n' \"$out\" >tmp/req-011/linux-desktop-rerender-path\nmkdir \"$out/source\"\ngit rev-parse HEAD >\"$out/source-sha\"\ngit diff --binary | shasum -a 256 >\"$out/diff-sha256\"\ngit ls-files -z --cached --others --exclude-standard | COPYFILE_DISABLE=1 tar -cf - --null -T - | tar -xf - -C \"$out/source\"\ncmp \"$old/source/frontend/package-lock.json\" \"$out/source/frontend/package-lock.json\"\ncp -cR \"$old/source/frontend/node_modules\" \"$out/source/frontend/\"\nmkdir -p \"$out/source/src-tauri/src/bin\"\ncp \"$old/source/src-tauri/src/bin/req011-driverless-loaded.rs\" \"$out/source/src-tauri/src/bin/\"\ncp \"$old\"/{run-isolated-x11.sh,run-native.sh,run-with-window-manager.sh,sample-family.py,summarize-native.py,compare-native-memory.py,reference-metadata.json} \"$out/\"\nshasum -a 256 \"$out/source/src-tauri/src/bin/req011-driverless-loaded.rs\" >\"$out/fixture-source.sha256\"\nwhile kill -0 93190 2>/dev/null; do sleep 8; done\ndocker run --rm --name req011-linux-desktop-rerender-build --cpus 3 -m 8g \\\n  -v \"$out/source:/candidate\" -v \"$cache/target:/cargo-target\" \\\n  -v \"$cache/cargo-registry:/usr/local/cargo/registry\" -v \"$out:/evidence\" \\\n  -e CARGO_TARGET_DIR=/cargo-target -w /candidate mesh-talk-req011-native-wm:local bash -ceu '\n    (cd frontend && npm run build)\n    cargo build --locked --release -j 2 -p mesh-talk --bin req011-driverless-loaded\n    cp /cargo-target/release/req011-driverless-loaded /evidence/\n    cd /evidence\n    sha256sum req011-driverless-loaded >native-binary.sha256\n  ' >\"$out/native-build.log\" 2>&1"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"failed","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":137,"duration":{"secs":898,"nanos":219691958}},"started_at_ms":1795409420342,"completed_at_ms":1795410318578}}
