{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T05:05:42.967Z","ordinal":36179,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0dca4931a04d8132016b03c9949d7087d0b4a851dd584f7ddc","status":"completed","call_id":"call_4882ce67b5824b81bf097660a5b634eb","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:`python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('docs/performance-requirements.md')\ns=p.read_text()\nneedle='## Apply to every feature'\ninsert='''## Headless post-office nodes\n\nApply the headless CPU and private-memory targets to the dedicated post-office\nprocess, including its attributable helpers. A relay stays available to receive\nconnections, serve mailbox requests and maintain required protocol leases while\nquiescent. Its steady idle work must remain bounded as retained ciphertext,\noffline participants and configured federation peers grow. An empty store alone\ncannot establish the retained-workload result.\n\n- At startup, restore only the indexes, authority and bounded cursors needed to\n  accept traffic. Keep migrations, backlog catch-up and recovery measurable\n  separately. Report time to accepting requests, peak memory and I/O.\n- In steady idle, wait for ingress, committed mailbox or topology changes and\n  the next real expiry, lease or retry deadline. Unchanged federation inventories,\n  empty drains and repeated unreachable peers must settle or back off. Sample\n  both an empty relay and a populated relay after warmup, including CPU, memory,\n  wakeups and disk writes. Observe the full hour to claim the write target.\n- Under traffic, measure delivery and custody latency, queue depth, memory,\n  CPU and I/O. Verify bounded batches, overload handling, restart recovery,\n  federation convergence and return to idle. Keep receipt meanings, retention,\n  authenticated scope and convergence guarantees intact.\n\nUse the existing [relay resource contracts](post-office-federation.md#indexed-relay-runtime-and-resource-bounds)\nand [event and scheduling owners](event-driven-design.md#schedule-work-by-purpose).\nRecord platform, binary, topology, load, sampling window and missing evidence\nalongside every result.\n\n'''\nassert s.count(needle)==1\np.write_text(s.replace(needle,insert+needle))\np=Path('docs/event-driven-design.md')\ns=p.read_text();needle='## Schedule work by purpose'\ninsert='''### Register relay work with its owner\n\nFor post-office work, identify the authoritative state transition and inspect\nthe existing mailbox, federation, topology or policy owner before creating a\nproducer. Register a scoped consumer with the existing event or watch if its\ncommit timing, identity and retirement semantics match. When those semantics\ndiffer, add the smallest event type to the owning module and document its scope,\ncoalescing, cancellation and reconciliation behavior.\n\nWhen there is no reliable event, register with the existing deadline, retry or\nrepair component described in [Scheduled work and recovery](scheduled-work.md).\nUse a cursor or bounded snapshot to repair missed events. Keep protocol\nheartbeats and lease deadlines with their protocol owner. Keep new threads or\nperiodic loops for cases where an existing component cannot meet the documented\ncontract. Verify that an empty or unchanged result parks, real work wakes\npromptly, and failures retain bounded retry and recovery.\n\n'''\nassert s.count(needle)==1\np.write_text(s.replace(needle,insert+needle))\np=Path('docs/post-office-federation.md')\ns=p.read_text();needle='## Indexed relay runtime and resource bounds\\\\n'\ns=s.replace(needle,needle+'''\nUse the [headless post-office performance requirements](performance-requirements.md#headless-post-office-nodes)\nfor startup, steady idle, active traffic and return-to-idle verification. Register\nnew reception, custody and federation work with its [event or scheduling owner](event-driven-design.md#register-relay-work-with-its-owner).\n''',1);p.write_text(s)\np=Path('AGENTS.md');s=p.read_text();needle='  rules when a confirmed defect reveals a new pattern.\\\\n'\ns=s.replace(needle,needle+'''  Apply the [headless post-office checklist](docs/performance-requirements.md#headless-post-office-nodes)\n  to relay changes and register background work with the\n  [existing event or scheduling owner](docs/event-driven-design.md#register-relay-work-with-its-owner).\n''',1);p.write_text(s)\nPY\ngit diff --check\nmake standards-check >tmp/req-011/post-office-doc-standards.log 2>&1`,yield_time_ms:1000}))\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a206ca-8bd3-7e61-8a39-400f1dbe0d63","create_time":1795410324.619389}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":15352,"sampled_through_sequence":15350,"client_authored":false,"model_search_state":"unused"}}
