{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T05:07:58.442Z","ordinal":36281,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0dca4931a04d8132016b03ca2ce5a087d085c6203a3b2dcbb4","status":"completed","call_id":"call_90578a95723d44afb57a101bf56800dc","name":"exec","input":"const r=await Promise.allSettled([tools.exec_command({cmd:\"sed -n '12,44p' docs/performance-requirements.md; git status --short | wc -l\"}),tools.mcp__english_pilot__english_coaching_context({})]);text(r[0].value.output);text(r[1].value.content[0].text.slice(0,450))\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a206cd-a4bf-7cc2-bbf1-f49e99f396ab","create_time":1795410476.899814}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":15384,"sampled_through_sequence":15381,"client_authored":false,"model_search_state":"unused"}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T05:07:58.592Z","ordinal":36282,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1feaf-24d9-7612-a284-664abd64a2c4","turn_id":"01a206cd-a4bf-7cc2-bbf1-f49e99f396ab","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-42cbf68a-3788-4f35-8789-1bcca5890768","process_id":"5130","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '12,44p' docs/performance-requirements.md; git status --short | wc -l"],"cwd":"file:///Users/kingsonwu/programming/OctopusGarage/mesh-talk","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"sed -n '12,44p' docs/performance-requirements.md; git status --short | wc -l"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"current application meets them**. Establish a production-build baseline on each\nsupported platform. Reference fixture: 4 logical CPUs, 8 GiB RAM, SSD, 100 contacts,\n20 groups and 100,000 stored messages; no pending transfers, calls or animations.\nSeparate cold start, warm start, catch-up, visible idle and hidden idle. Measure a\nquiet five-minute window after warmup; record build, runtime, profile and workload.\nWarm startup restarts the process with OS caches retained; cold startup records\nits uncached/first-launch conditions. Usable means an actionable list or\nconversation, not a blank shell; report human authorization waits separately.\nThe empty-shell comparison keeps the same backend, runtime, process membership\nand window settings, with user payloads absent.\n\n| Resource                | Initial target for the reference fixture                                                                                                                                                            |\n| ----------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Idle CPU                | Visible desktop: ≤1% of one logical CPU; hidden desktop: ≤0.25%; headless node: ≤0.5%, averaged over the window.                                                                                    |\n| Retained memory         | Headless node: ≤64 MiB private commit. Desktop: ≤64 MiB workload delta above the same-build empty shell; establish a reviewed whole-family ceiling from that baseline.                              |\n| Memory growth           | Repeated navigation/media cycles reach a bounded plateau. Tenfold stored history must not require tenfold startup reads or retained UI payloads.                                                    |\n| Idle writes             | Zero business-data commits for unchanged inputs. Target ≤5 MiB/hour OS-observed attributable storage writes per application family after warmup; measure the full hour before claiming this target. |\n| Background wakeups      | No application maintenance timer without pending work, a real deadline or a documented recovery purpose. Noncritical recovery defaults to ≥5 minutes and coalesces activation.                      |\n| Startup and interaction | First usable shell ≤1 s warm / ≤3 s cold; ordinary interaction must not run blocking I/O, crypto or an unbounded traversal on the UI thread. Report hydration/catch-up separately.                  |\n\nCPU means `100 × process CPU seconds / wall seconds`, summed over the full app\nfamily; divide by logical CPU count only when reporting whole-machine percent.\nReport Rust host **and** renderer/GPU/helpers. Distinguish private commit, private\nresident memory, shared pages and live JS heap; on Linux use PSS for shared-page\nattribution. Logical I/O includes IPC/network activity and is not physical disk\nI/O; OS disk events also do not measure physical NAND write amplification. CPU alone does not establish battery/power efficiency: inspect wakeups, GPU,\nnetwork and actual energy where supported. Keep metrics collected in different\nwindows separate. Store measurements in PR/CI artifacts, not this guide.\n\nAn existing target miss requires recorded baseline and an owned follow-up; it is\nnot permission to worsen the path or silently raise its budget. A target change\nrequires comparable evidence and review. Migrations, catch-up and active media have\nseparate bounded work budgets and progress evidence, not an unlimited exception.\n      83\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":10375}},"started_at_ms":1795410478592,"completed_at_ms":1795410478592}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T05:07:58.726Z","ordinal":36283,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a1feaf-24d9-7612-a284-664abd64a2c4","turn_id":"01a206cd-a4bf-7cc2-bbf1-f49e99f396ab","session_id":"01a1feaf-24d9-7612-a284-664abd64a2c4","root_turn_id":"01a206cd-a4bf-7cc2-bbf1-f49e99f396ab","response_id":"resp_0dca4931a04d8132016b03ca28502887d0a2a56a4b7870240e","usage":{"input_tokens":344624,"cached_input_tokens":344448,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":165,"reasoning_output_tokens":31,"total_tokens":344789},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":344624,"cached_input_tokens":344448,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":165,"reasoning_output_tokens":31,"total_tokens":344789},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":1284548659,"cached_input_tokens":1279188096,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1133107,"reasoning_output_tokens":298741,"total_tokens":1285681766}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T05:07:59.244Z","ordinal":36284,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1feaf-24d9-7612-a284-664abd64a2c4","turn_id":"01a206cd-a4bf-7cc2-bbf1-f49e99f396ab","item":{"type":"McpToolCall","id":"exec-65843382-a681-46bc-bd92-1ba8b64b32c8","server":"english-pilot","tool":"english_coaching_context","arguments":{},"status":"completed","result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"guidance\": \"Do not derail the user's main task. Enforce mode is enabled: over-threshold prompts are handled by the submit hook before the agent turn. Force mode is enabled: append one English note using the configured note depth whenever the prompt has Chinese fragments, non-native phrasing, or a clearly better everyday expression. Prefer practical workplace English, brief teaching rationale, and reusable expressions.\",\n  \"finalResponseInstruction\": \"Finish the main task first. For the latest allowed user prompt, append one English note using the configured note depth if it contains any Chinese fragment, awkward English, or obvious phrasing improvement: Use a Rich English Note by default: 5-8 useful lines, brief enough for a final response but rich enough for study.\\nUse this shape:\\nEnglish note:\\nOriginal: \\\"fix this problem\\\"\\nBetter: \\\"fix this issue\\\" / \\\"resolve this startup issue\\\"\\nWhy: In engineering conversations, \\\"issue\\\" is more precise than \\\"problem\\\" when discussing bugs, failures, tickets, or startup errors.\\nUseful patterns:\\n- \\\"The MCP client failed during the startup handshake.\\\"\\n- \\\"This issue belongs at the config boundary, not the runtime path.\\\"\\nCollocations: startup issue, handshake failure, config mismatch, reproduce the issue, verify the fix\\nCommon mistake: Use \\\"problem\\\" for general trouble; use \\\"issue\\\" for bugs, tickets, incidents, and engineering discussions.\\nIPA: issue /ˈɪʃuː/ or /ˈɪsjuː/ For programming-task conversations, prefer software-engineering English in the final note. Good sentence patterns: append an English note at the end; keep the behavior behind a small interface; make the failure path explicit; cache the result to avoid repeating the same expensive operation; this change belongs at the module boundary. Use the configured computer-English files as vocabulary hints, not as text to quote every time.\",\n  \"domainReference\": {\n    \"style\": \"software-engineering\",\n    \"available\": false,\n    \"terms\": [],\n    \"examples\": [\n      \"append an English note at the end\",\n      \"keep the behavior behind a small interface\",\n      \"make the failure path explicit\",\n      \"cache the result to avoid repeating the same expensive operation\",\n      \"this change belongs at the module boundary\"\n    ],\n    \"missingPaths\": []\n  },\n  \"cadence\": \"Force mode bypasses cooldown and daily-cap intent for teachable user prompts; follow the configured note depth and keep the note professional. Skip only when there is no meaningful wording improvement.\",\n  \"policy\": {\n    \"gateMode\": \"enforce\",\n    \"intensity\": \"force\",\n    \"cooldownMinutes\": 0,\n    \"maxInlineCoachingPerDay\": 999,\n    \"assistantEnglishNoteDepth\": \"rich\"\n  },\n  \"today\": {\n    \"date\": \"2026-11-23\",\n    \"coachingShown\": 0,\n    \"remaining\": 999\n  },\n  \"cooldown\": {\n    \"active\": false,\n    \"lastShownAt\": \"2026-08-01T13:52:28.084Z\"\n  },\n  \"decision\": {\n    \"shouldOfferInlineCoaching\": true,\n    \"reason\": \"available\"\n  }\n}"}]},"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":601704583}},"started_at_ms":1795410478642,"completed_at_ms":1795410479244}}
