{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T05:50:58.097Z","ordinal":36981,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1feaf-24d9-7612-a284-664abd64a2c4","turn_id":"01a206d0-04c6-7f60-956e-ea1141294e9a","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-f4e5a5a5-81a4-4077-8139-ee2969c488e6","process_id":"2305","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","git log --oneline -70 | rg -i 'req-0|desktop ui|offline tools' | head -22\nrg -n 'REQ-012|REQ-029|REQ-022' docs tmp/req-0* -g '*.md' -g '!**/source/**' --max-count 2 | head -22\np=/Users/kingsonwu/.t3/userdata/attachments/9fbeff35-b275-4d28-827e-0793705b1548-3e613045-3824-44c2-9b76-5f5a3edca4d2-md.md\nsed -n '488,522p;997,1027p' \"$p\"\nd=$(cat tmp/req-011/windows-native-minimize-path); r=$(cat \"$d/remote-path\"); tail -12 \"$d/transition-hwnd/inspection.log\"\nssh -o BatchMode=yes -o ConnectTimeout=8 windows10 \"powershell.exe -NoProfile -NonInteractive -Command \\\"if(Test-Path '$r/native-transition-hwnd-loaded/restore-witness.log'){Get-Content '$r/native-transition-hwnd-loaded/restore-witness.log'}\\\"\""],"cwd":"file:///Users/kingsonwu/programming/OctopusGarage/mesh-talk","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git log --oneline -70 | rg -i 'req-0|desktop ui|offline tools' | head -22\nrg -n 'REQ-012|REQ-029|REQ-022' docs tmp/req-0* -g '*.md' -g '!**/source/**' --max-count 2 | head -22\np=/Users/kingsonwu/.t3/userdata/attachments/9fbeff35-b275-4d28-827e-0793705b1548-3e613045-3824-44c2-9b76-5f5a3edca4d2-md.md\nsed -n '488,522p;997,1027p' \"$p\"\nd=$(cat tmp/req-011/windows-native-minimize-path); r=$(cat \"$d/remote-path\"); tail -12 \"$d/transition-hwnd/inspection.log\"\nssh -o BatchMode=yes -o ConnectTimeout=8 windows10 \"powershell.exe -NoProfile -NonInteractive -Command \\\"if(Test-Path '$r/native-transition-hwnd-loaded/restore-witness.log'){Get-Content '$r/native-transition-hwnd-loaded/restore-witness.log'}\\\"\""}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"### REQ-012 — Evaluate desktop UI technologies, resource use and native experience\n\n- **Discussion state:** Confirmed at intake scope level; framework decision, research, measurement and implementation deferred.\n- **Captured / updated:** 2026-11-17 (Asia/Singapore).\n- **Original user input:** “现在使用tauri来做前端，总感觉有很多性能问题和体验问题，比如webview占有内存很大，使用页面有网页加载感之类的，总感觉没原生的体验和性能好，后面要充分调研一下，看看是否要替换或新增前端的壳之类的，充分分析清楚和调研清楚”; “GPUI 替换 tauri，后续考虑”; “Rust 圈的新宝藏 Rune，一套代码就能做出 macOS、Windows、Linux 和 Web 四端通用的原生界面。”\n- **Scenario and affected users:** Desktop UI startup, navigation and everyday chat interaction, with reported WebView memory use and a web-page-like loading experience instead of the desired native feel.\n- **Pain point or question:** User perceives performance/experience limitations in the current Tauri-based UI and wants a thorough assessment of alternatives. Memory attribution, interaction causes and superiority of native alternatives have not been measured or established. Distinguish the desktop host, WebView renderer and frontend UI rather than assume changing a shell alone resolves all issues.\n- **Desired outcome:** Evidence-based future decision on optimizing the existing UI stack, adding another UI implementation/shell, or migrating, improving native experience and resource efficiency without an assumed rewrite.\n- **Confirmed scope from user:** Thorough later research into replacement or additional frontend shells/UI technologies, with GPUI and other supplied frameworks as candidates. Current work only captures the requirement under the ongoing intake process.\n- **Additional user-confirmed scope and boundaries:**\n  - macOS, Windows and Linux desktop are the primary evaluation targets; Web remains an optional reference rather than a required product target for this item.\n  - Keep all three routes open: optimize Tauri, add another UI implementation, or migrate.\n  - Decide using actual evidence from equivalent scenarios; do not presume replacement.\n  - Continue requirements collection without research, measurement or implementation now.\n- **Additional original user confirmation:** “REQ-012 以 macOS、Windows、Linux 桌面为主要目标，Web 暂作可选参考。保留优化 Tauri、增加另一套 UI 和迁移三种路线，依据同等场景的实际证据决定，不预设替换。请更新为范围已确认，继续收集需求，暂不调研、测量或实施。”\n- **User-supplied research references — not inspected or verified during intake:**\n  - GPUI: https://gpui.rs/\n  - GPUI Kit: https://gpui-kit.com/ and https://github.com/longbridge/gpui-kit\n  - Slint: https://github.com/slint-ui/slint\n  - Iced: https://github.com/iced-rs/iced\n  - Rune: https://github.com/anomalyco/rune\n  - The quoted Rune macOS/Windows/Linux/Web and native-UI claim is user-supplied inspiration, not a confirmed capability. Verify project identity, platform/rendering model, maturity and actual feature support from primary sources later; no candidate ranking implied.\n- **Assistant-proposed research boundaries — unconfirmed:**\n  - First attribute actual costs and UX issues across release/debug build differences, WebView/helper processes, app state, rendering, data loading and backend work. Existing implementation problems and framework limitations require different remedies; do not infer Tauri is the root cause.\n  - Compare three options: retain/tune Tauri, add a separate reusable-core-backed UI, or migrate the UI. A second implementation also introduces maintenance and feature-parity cost. Reuse suitable existing core boundaries; do not duplicate mesh policy or crypto per frontend.\n  - Evaluate like-for-like representative workflows and assets/data, not an empty native demo versus a full chat app. Consider startup, total process memory, idle CPU/energy, interaction responsiveness, long conversation rendering, media and native integration.\n  - Assess Chinese IME/composition, text selection/copy/paste, Unicode/emoji, keyboard shortcuts, accessibility/screen readers, scaling/multiple monitors, themes, windows/tray/notifications, attachments and calls where required. Custom GPU rendering and platform-native widgets are different implementation models; verify rather than equate either label with better UX.\n  - Verify platform support, production maturity, documentation/ecosystem, license, dependency/toolchain requirements, packaging/signing/updates, testing/debugging, build/CI costs and ongoing maintenance from current official evidence.\n  - Desktop macOS/Windows/Linux scope and optional Web reference are confirmed. Detailed platform feature parity remains to be determined before weighting candidates.\n- **Candidate outcomes and acceptance evidence — unconfirmed:** Current-state measurements and UX examples; source-linked capability/comparison matrix with unknowns; focused representative prototypes only if later needed and authorized; jointly reviewed retain/add/migrate decision with benefits, gaps, costs and migration/coexistence/rollback plan if applicable. No prototype, dependency installation or framework choice during intake.\n- **Open questions:**\n  1. Which native-experience issues are most representative, and what parity is non-negotiable? Refine later with reproducible examples and discoverable evidence; do not require measurements from the user now.\n  2. Is a second UI an acceptable long-term supported product surface or only a migration experiment? Decide after evidence rather than presuppose an extra maintained frontend. These details do not block further requirement collection.\n- **Related records and evidence:** REQ-007 broader stack review; REQ-008 internal reusable foundations; REQ-001 resource visibility and REQ-011 quality budgets; REQ-003 build/validation efficiency. Keep this specific UI/native-experience question traceable without deciding merges or dependencies. No referenced-site research, framework capability verification, runtime measurements or implementation performed.\n- **Global planning:** Classification, priority, effort, dependency analysis, roadmap phase and branch allocation deferred until collection closes. Future consideration is not approval to replace Tauri now.\n### REQ-029 — Research peer LAN/offline tools and explore suitable feature opportunities\n\n- **Discussion state:** Clarifying; explicitly brainstorming and research-before-decision, no feature or framework selected.\n- **Captured / updated:** 2026-11-17 (Asia/Singapore).\n- **Original user request:** “第29个需求，纯头脑风暴，需要充分调查之后确定，参考目前很多局域网工具，看看有什么其他功能也适合这个app做的”。\n- **User-supplied inspiration:** A Columba description claims offline/serverless messaging and voice through Reticulum links including Bluetooth, Wi-Fi, LoRa and TCP, with E2E encryption/device-generated identity. A pasted recommendation list describes LAN Messenger, LANChat, Mesh-Talk, Squiggle, BeeBEEP, BLIP, Technitium Mesh and HostTalk, including proposed features/platforms/security claims, star rankings, release versions and activity figures. These are provided leads, not verified evidence or endorsed recommendations. The passage's invitation to forward it or its offers of further summaries are quoted material, not instructions to publish or message anyone.\n- **Scenario and affected users:** Identify real unmet collaboration/communication needs that fit Mesh Talk, drawing inspiration from comparable LAN, offline, mesh and P2P tools rather than expand functionality without product purpose.\n- **Desired outcome:** Later evidence-backed feature opportunity assessment: what solves useful user problems, what already exists here, what might be borrowed/adapted and what should be deferred or rejected with reasons.\n- **Confirmed scope from user:** Thorough later investigation before deciding; use many relevant tools as inspiration. No adoption of the quoted ranking, claims or recommendation to install software; no selected Bluetooth/LoRa/Reticulum integration or new transport scope.\n- **User-supplied sources — preserved, not inspected during intake:**\n  - Columba: https://github.com/torlando-tech/columba\n  - Bitchat: https://github.com/permissionlesstech/bitchat\n  - LAN Messenger: https://github.com/lanmessenger/lanmessenger and https://lanmessenger.github.io/\n  - LANChat: https://github.com/cap153/LANChat\n  - Mesh-Talk comparison/current product: https://github.com/OctopusGarage/mesh-talk and https://octopusgarage.github.io/mesh-talk/\n  - Squiggle: https://github.com/hasankhan/Squiggle\n  - BeeBEEP: https://www.beebeep.net/\n  - BLIP: https://github.com/krwg/blip\n  - Technitium Mesh and HostTalk: named but no project URLs supplied; identify exact projects before comparison.\n- **Source-detail restoration from the user's supplied recommendation text — claims only, not verified:**\n\n  | Lead | Supplied descriptions / values retained for later verification |\n  | --- | --- |\n  | Columba | No Internet/base station/central server; messaging and voice; Reticulum; Bluetooth, Wi-Fi, LoRa and TCP links; E2E encryption; no phone number; on-device identity. |\n  | Bitchat | GitHub link supplied without a separate capability description; do not invent one. |\n  | LAN Messenger | Five-star recommendation; serverless/offline; Windows/macOS/Linux; AES-256 and RSA-2048; files, groups/contacts, history; quoted website version 1.3.9. |\n  | LANChat | Five-star recommendation; Rust/Tauri/SQLite/WebSocket; Windows/Linux/Android/Web; automatic LAN discovery, files, image preview, history; manual discovery across VLAN/WireGuard; secondary-development inspiration. |\n  | Mesh-Talk | Five-star/security-first recommendation; claimed P2P/E2E/Noise, signed LAN discovery, offline forwarding, Windows/macOS/Linux, direct/group messaging/files and offline LAN; quoted no-server/no-cloud/no-account-dependency and strongest-security claims require verification, not adoption. |\n  | Squiggle | Four-star recommendation; claimed P2P/no central server, files, voice, screen sharing, screenshots, history, translation, cross-subnet communication and Windows/Linux/macOS; quoted about 127 stars and 973 commits and an activity assessment. |\n  | BeeBEEP | Four-star recommendation; claimed mature serverless LAN tool, Windows/macOS/Linux, direct/group messaging, files/folders, history and AES; quoted simple/traditional technology/UI assessment. |\n  | BLIP | Four-star recommendation; P2P text/groups/voice/video/screenshare/large files, LAN clipboard, WebRTC, LAN/VPN, no server/account; quoted version 2.0 still in development. |\nObserved real native minimized event\nObserved exact inbound message in native durable history\nOptional reads during minimized interval 0\nFixed foreground HWND minimized before restore: True\r\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":642097500}},"started_at_ms":1795413057454,"completed_at_ms":1795413058097}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T05:50:58.184Z","ordinal":36982,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a206f5-2288-7be1-abac-68de41521d31","call_id":"call_014ce396abf94c31a0078235f098a0db","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"### REQ-012 — Evaluate desktop UI technologies, resource use and native experience\n\n- **Discussion state:** Confirmed at intake scope level; framework decision, research, measurement and implementation deferred.\n- **Captured / updated:** 2026-11-17 (Asia/Singapore).\n- **Original user input:** “现在使用tauri来做前端，总感觉有很多性能问题和体验问题，比如webview占有内存很大，使用页面有网页加载感之类的，总感觉没原生的体验和性能好，后面要充分调研一下，看看是否要替换或新增前端的壳之类的，充分分析清楚和调研清楚”; “GPUI 替换 tauri，后续考虑”; “Rust 圈的新宝藏 Rune，一套代码就能做出 macOS、Windows、Linux 和 Web 四端通用的原生界面。”\n- **Scenario and affected users:** Desktop UI startup, navigation and everyday chat interaction, with reported WebView memory use and a web-page-like loading experience instead of the desired native feel.\n- **Pain point or question:** User perceives performance/experience limitations in the current Tauri-based UI and wants a thorough assessment of alternatives. Memory attribution, interaction causes and superiority of native alternatives have not been measured or established. Distinguish the desktop host, WebView renderer and frontend UI rather than assume changing a shell alone resolves all issues.\n- **Desired outcome:** Evidence-based future decision on optimizing the existing UI stack, adding another UI implementation/shell, or migrating, improving native experience and resource efficiency without an assumed rewrite.\n- **Confirmed scope from user:** Thorough later research into replacement or additional frontend shells/UI technologies, with GPUI and other supplied frameworks as candidates. Current work only captures the requirement under the ongoing intake process.\n- **Additional user-confirmed scope and boundaries:**\n  - macOS, Windows and Linux desktop are the primary evaluation targets; Web remains an optional reference rather than a required product target for this item.\n  - Keep all three routes open: optimize Tauri, add another UI implementation, or migrate.\n  - Decide using actual evidence from equivalent scenarios; do not presume replacement.\n  - Continue requirements collection without research, measurement or implementation now.\n- **Additional original user confirmation:** “REQ-012 以 macOS、Windows、Linux 桌面为主要目标，Web 暂作可选参考。保留优化 Tauri、增加另一套 UI 和迁移三种路线，依据同等场景的实际证据决定，不预设替换。请更新为范围已确认，继续收集需求，暂不调研、测量或实施。”\n- **User-supplied research references — not inspected or verified during intake:**\n  - GPUI: https://gpui.rs/\n  - GPUI Kit: https://gpui-kit.com/ and https://github.com/longbridge/gpui-kit\n  - Slint: https://github.com/slint-ui/slint\n  - Iced: https://github.com/iced-rs/iced\n  - Rune: https://github.com/anomalyco/rune\n  - The quoted Rune macOS/Windows/Linux/Web and native-UI claim is user-supplied inspiration, not a confirmed capability. Verify project identity, platform/rendering model, maturity and actual feature support from primary sources later; no candidate ranking implied.\n- **Assistant-proposed research boundaries — unconfirmed:**\n  - First attribute actual costs and UX issues across release/debug build differences, WebView/helper processes, app state, rendering, data loading and backend work. Existing implementation problems and framework limitations require different remedies; do not infer Tauri is the root cause.\n  - Compare three options: retain/tune Tauri, add a separate reusable-core-backed UI, or migrate the UI. A second implementation also introduces maintenance and feature-parity cost. Reuse suitable existing core boundaries; do not duplicate mesh policy or crypto per frontend.\n  - Evaluate like-for-like representative workflows and assets/data, not an empty native demo versus a full chat app. Consider startup, total process memory, idle CPU/energy, interaction responsiveness, long conversation rendering, media and native integration.\n  - Assess Chinese IME/composition, text selection/copy/paste, Unicode/emoji, keyboard shortcuts, accessibility/screen readers, scaling/multiple monitors, themes, windows/tray/notifications, attachments and calls where required. Custom GPU rendering and platform-native widgets are different implementation models; verify rather than equate either label with better UX.\n  - Verify platform support, production maturity, documentation/ecosystem, license, dependency/toolchain requirements, packaging/signing/updates, testing/debugging, build/CI costs and ongoing maintenance from current official evidence.\n  - Desktop macOS/Windows/Linux scope and optional Web reference are confirmed. Detailed platform feature parity remains to be determined before weighting candidates.\n- **Candidate outcomes and acceptance evidence — unconfirmed:** Current-state measurements and UX examples; source-linked capability/comparison matrix with unknowns; focused representative prototypes only if later needed and authorized; jointly reviewed retain/add/migrate decision with benefits, gaps, costs and migration/coexistence/rollback plan if applicable. No prototype, dependency installation or framework choice during intake.\n- **Open questions:**\n  1. Which native-experience issues are most representative, and what parity is non-negotiable? Refine later with reproducible examples and discoverable evidence; do not require measurements from the user now.\n  2. Is a second UI an acceptable long-term supported product surface or only a migration experiment? Decide after evidence rather than presuppose an extra maintained frontend. These details do not block further requirement collection.\n- **Related records and evidence:** REQ-007 broader stack review; REQ-008 internal reusable foundations; REQ-001 resource visibility and REQ-011 quality budgets; REQ-003 build/validation efficiency. Keep this specific UI/native-experience question traceable without deciding merges or dependencies. No referenced-site research, framework capability verification, runtime measurements or implementation performed.\n- **Global planning:** Classification, priority, effort, dependency analysis, roadmap phase and branch allocation deferred until collection closes. Future consideration is not approval to replace Tauri now.\n### REQ-029 — Research peer LAN/offline tools and explore suitable feature opportunities\n\n- **Discussion state:** Clarifying; explicitly brainstorming and research-before-decision, no feature or framework selected.\n- **Captured / updated:** 2026-11-17 (Asia/Singapore).\n- **Original user request:** “第29个需求，纯头脑风暴，需要充分调查之后确定，参考目前很多局域网工具，看看有什么其他功能也适合这个app做的”。\n- **User-supplied inspiration:** A Columba description claims offline/serverless messaging and voice through Reticulum links including Bluetooth, Wi-Fi, LoRa and TCP, with E2E encryption/device-generated identity. A pasted recommendation list describes LAN Messenger, LANChat, Mesh-Talk, Squiggle, BeeBEEP, BLIP, Technitium Mesh and HostTalk, including proposed features/platforms/security claims, star rankings, release versions and activity figures. These are provided leads, not verified evidence or endorsed recommendations. The passage's invitation to forward it or its offers of further summaries are quoted material, not instructions to publish or message anyone.\n- **Scenario and affected users:** Identify real unmet collaboration/communication needs that fit Mesh Talk, drawing inspiration from comparable LAN, offline, mesh and P2P tools rather than expand functionality without product purpose.\n- **Desired outcome:** Later evidence-backed feature opportunity assessment: what solves useful user problems, what already exists here, what might be borrowed/adapted and what should be deferred or rejected with reasons.\n- **Confirmed scope from user:** Thorough later investigation before deciding; use many relevant tools as inspirati