{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T06:10:50.285Z","ordinal":37369,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a20707-532d-7dd2-a9c0-d5d288b51f82","call_id":"call_103083dae27c47e4b438f41a67422a46","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.9 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Globals | Microsoft Learn (https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-edge/webview2/reference/win32/webview2-idl?view=webview2-1.0.4258.31)\nciteturn26search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; You may specify the `userDataFolder` to change the default user data folder location for WebView2. ... If you find an override environment variable, use the `browserExecutableFolder` and `userDataFolder` values as replacements for the corresponding values in `CreateCoreWebView2EnvironmentWithOptions` parameters. ... While not strictly overrides, additional environment variables may be set.\n\nThe `browserExecutableFolder`, `channelSearchKind`, `releaseChannels`, `userDataFolder` and `additionalBrowserArguments` of the `environmentOptions` may be overridden by values either specified in environment variables or in the registry.\n\nWhen creating a `WebView2Environment` the following environment variables are verified.\n\ntext\n\nCopy\n    \n    `WEBVIEW2_BROWSER_EXECUTABLE_FOLDER\n    WEBVIEW2_USER_DATA_FOLDER\n    WEBVIEW2_ADDITIONAL_BROWSER_ARGUMENTS\n    WEBVIEW2_CHANNEL_SEARCH_KIND\n    WEBVIEW2_RELEASE_CHANNELS\n    `\n\nIf you find an override environment variable, use the `browserExecutableFolder` and `userDataFolder` values as replacements for the corresponding values in `CreateCoreWebView2EnvironmentWithOptions` parameters. If `additionalBrowserArguments` is specified in environment variable or in the registry, it is appended to the corresponding values in `CreateCoreWebView2EnvironmentWithOptions` parameters. See `ReleaseChannels` on ICoreWebView2EnvironmentOptions for more details on how to construct the registry key and environment variable values.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGlobals | Microsoft Learn (https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-edge/webview2/reference/win32/webview2-idl?view=webview2-1.0.3967.48)\nciteturn26search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago; You may specify the `userDataFolder` to change the default user data folder location for WebView2. ... If you find an override environment variable, use the `browserExecutableFolder` and `userDataFolder` values as replacements for the corresponding values in `CreateCoreWebView2EnvironmentWithOptions` parameters. ... While not strictly overrides, additio"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a20706-0b66-75d1-a839-57280589689c","create_time":1795414250.285863}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":15857,"sampled_through_sequence":15854,"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000,"model_search_state":"unused"}}
