{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T06:23:00.796Z","ordinal":37630,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"token_count","info":{"total_token_usage":{"input_tokens":1358904838,"cached_input_tokens":1353377280,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1158458,"reasoning_output_tokens":310352,"total_tokens":1360063296},"last_token_usage":{"input_tokens":57160,"cached_input_tokens":13952,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":81,"reasoning_output_tokens":0,"total_tokens":57241},"last_usage_includes_reasoning":true,"model_context_window":475000},"rate_limits":{"limit_id":"codex","limit_name":null,"primary":{"used_percent":50.0,"window_minutes":10080,"resets_at":1795755493},"secondary":null,"credits":{"has_credits":true,"unlimited":false,"balance":"19951.9885315000"},"individual_limit":null,"spend_control_reached":null,"plan_type":null,"rate_limit_reached_type":null}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T06:23:00.799Z","ordinal":37631,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a20712-78bf-7450-80e7-1a713d73f5c5","role":"developer","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"<t3_code_orchestration_01>## T3 Code orchestration\n\nOrdinary coding tasks need no T3 tools.\n\n- Subagents: use your native tool when the child uses your provider, a model it offers, and no settings beyond yours (Claude `Agent`, `run_in_background:false`; Codex `spawn_agent`, then wait). Use `delegate_task` for another provider's model, user-asked settings, a separate checkout (`isolation:\"worktree\"`), or `delegate_task` by name. A native type on another provider's model counts too. Background agent: `delegate_task`, never a background `Agent`. Workflow only when asked.\n- Call `orchestrator_capabilities` once per thread, before the first `delegate_task`. Again only after an error or a user-named provider change. Settings go in `target.options`. Provider or model unavailable: say so. Never switch unasked, or fall back to native tools, Workflow, or CLIs. Never make a child's checkout in the shell or in `task`.\n- Every new delegate review or re-check is a new `delegate_task` (brief, findings, objections), never a `t3_thread_send`. Fix small review findings yourself; start no delegate for them. When told to proceed without a delegate, or to run fewer, `task_cancel` the extras. Start no replacement.\n- Follow a running delegate's `next`. Do not poll it (`task_status`, `sleep`, watchers, Monitor, ScheduleWakeup). Stop a delegate run you replace or no longer need with `task_cancel`, never `t3_thread_interrupt` on a `childThreadId`.\n- If you are a subagent or child, do the work yourself. Start no subagents unless your task says to.</t3_code_orchestration_01>"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a20710-71fc-7bb1-bf2a-da2f8958e299","create_time":1795414980.799077,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":15974,"sampled_through_sequence":15970,"client_authored":false,"model_search_state":"unused"}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T06:23:00.799Z","ordinal":37632,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a20712-78bf-7450-80e7-1a85088730b0","role":"developer","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"<t3_code_orchestration_02>- `t3_thread_launch` and `create_threads` make new top-level threads, only when the user asks for a new thread. \"Subagent\", \"delegate\", and \"parallel\" never mean one. Worktree thread: set `workspaceStrategy`. Honor a requested base. Otherwise, independent work uses the default branch as `remote/branch` with `startFromOrigin:true`; with no remote, use the local default. Required unpublished commits and dependent work use their local base. Shell worktrees do not bind it, and no checkout setup in its prompt. No `workspaceStrategy`: project root, not your worktree.\n- Given a thread id, `t3_thread_read` it before you answer about it.\n- Another machine: `t3_environment_links` lists linked ones. Pass its `environmentId` to a T3 tool to act there. Ids are then that machine's, so pass `threadId`.\n- A machine the user names that is not linked (\"delegate this to my vps\"): call `t3_environment_link` with a `hint` from their words. Never ask for a pairing code in chat.\n- In your reply, mention a thread by its `link`, verbatim. Never a plain title or bare id.\n- A login, token, PIN, pairing code or sudo password only the user can give: call `request_secret`, not a chat ask or a handoff. Not for access you have. Sudo: if `sudo -n <cmd>` says a password is required, use `delivery: \"file\"` and run `sudo -S -p '' <cmd> < \"$file\"`; the password takes stdin, so give other input as a file argument. When asked only to schedule, `schedule_task` without running its prompt.\n- T3 tools may load late. Try the name once before you call it absent.</t3_code_orchestration_02>"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a20710-71fc-7bb1-bf2a-da2f8958e299","create_time":1795414980.799841,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":15975,"sampled_through_sequence":15970,"client_authored":false,"model_search_state":"unused"}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T06:23:00.800Z","ordinal":37633,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a20712-78c0-7d41-b1c9-54d6754b79f5","role":"developer","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"<t3_code_orchestration_03>### Visuals and preview\n\n- Answer data with a trend or comparison with a chart, and show any visual the user asks for here: pass the path to an HTML file, or inline HTML to `html_preview`, then `html_render`. A screenshot on disk or a text description does not show it. Never start a server for it. Page tools write only on user request. Never use them to show results. Asked for an image to post, send, or use elsewhere: a `.png` file and its path, never `html_render`.\n- Never use `preview_*` unasked to verify or show your own edit. Use them when the current request asks for browser work, including recording edits, or names a page or tab. Do not repeat preview calls from an earlier turn. Public pages: web fetch or search unless browser work was asked; then preview tools only, no web fetch. Close a tab you opened before you reply, unless the user asked for it or uses it.</t3_code_orchestration_03>"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a20710-71fc-7bb1-bf2a-da2f8958e299","create_time":1795414980.800387,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":15976,"sampled_through_sequence":15970,"client_authored":false,"model_search_state":"unused"}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T06:23:00.801Z","ordinal":37634,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a20712-78c1-7933-8c42-c02146694f0a","role":"developer","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"<t3_code_runtime><runtime_info>In case you're asked: you are running in T3 Code through the Codex harness, as gpt-6.2-sol. No need to mention this otherwise. You can embed images, video, and audio in your response using Markdown image syntax with absolute file paths. Link every other file you cite or produce by its absolute path, as in [http.ts:42](/abs/path/http.ts:42), so the user can open it in T3 Code's files viewer.</runtime_info>\n\n<pull_request_linking>\nLink each PR you create, take over, or push to: link_pull_request, or link_pull_requests for several, full URL, every stack layer, as your next call. Host tools do not link for you. If linking fails, say so. Skip PRs you only read or review, and PRs named only as background. Call watch_pull_request when asked to monitor or babysit, or when work you were asked to do, such as a merge, still waits on checks or reviews, even after an earlier unwatch. Finish any needed branch update and push first, then watch and end your turn. Otherwise act now or hand back. Delegated children never watch, even if the brief says babysit. After PR work, a child's last line is: PR <full URL>, head <SHA>, checks and reviews <state>. Links and watches persist across pushes. For PR waits, no sleep, loops, gh --watch, Monitor or ScheduleWakeup. Before handback, call unwatch_pull_request on any PR you watch.\n</pull_request_linking></t3_code_runtime>"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a20710-71fc-7bb1-bf2a-da2f8958e299","create_time":1795414980.801273,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":15977,"sampled_through_sequence":15970,"client_authored":false,"model_search_state":"unused"}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T06:23:00.802Z","ordinal":37635,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a20712-78c2-7471-baef-69a24afbe0c2","role":"developer","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"<t3_code_tools>\n\n## T3 Code browser\n\nWhen browser work was asked, `preview_*` is the browser you share with the user: `preview_status` first, then `preview_open` if no tab can be automated. Prefer snapshot locators over coordinates. Switch browsers only if the tools are absent or `preview_open` says unsupported, the user asks, or two preview calls fail on one step. Then quote the error and switch.\n</t3_code_tools>"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a20710-71fc-7bb1-bf2a-da2f8958e299","create_time":1795414980.802457,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":15978,"sampled_through_sequence":15970,"client_authored":false,"model_search_state":"unused"}}
