{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T06:25:25.537Z","ordinal":37763,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1feaf-24d9-7612-a284-664abd64a2c4","turn_id":"01a20714-7670-7992-bc75-1b8771ae748b","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-88a64309-fc4b-4836-9b9e-dad3e660c6cc","process_id":"32947","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n 'channelMembers\\(' frontend/src --glob '!*.test.*'\nrg -n 'channel_members\\(' src-tauri/src \nsed -n '194,292p' src-tauri/src/chat_commands/channels.rs\nsed -n '130,190p' frontend/src/store/channelRefresh.ts\nrg -n 'struct ChannelMembersInfo' src-tauri/src/chat_commands/channels.rs\nsed -n '1,30p' docs/module-boundaries.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/kingsonwu/programming/OctopusGarage/mesh-talk","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n \"channelMembers\\\\(\" frontend/src --glob '!*.test.*'","query":"channelMembers\\(","path":"frontend"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n \"channel_members\\\\(\" src-tauri/src","query":"channel_members\\(","path":"src-tauri"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '194,292p' src-tauri/src/chat_commands/channels.rs","name":"channels.rs","path":"src-tauri/src/chat_commands/channels.rs"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '130,190p' frontend/src/store/channelRefresh.ts","name":"channelRefresh.ts","path":"frontend/src/store/channelRefresh.ts"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'struct ChannelMembersInfo' src-tauri/src/chat_commands/channels.rs","query":"struct ChannelMembersInfo","path":"channels.rs"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,30p' docs/module-boundaries.md","name":"module-boundaries.md","path":"docs/module-boundaries.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"frontend/src/store/channelRefresh.ts:29:    channelMembers(id: string): Promise<ChannelMembersInfo>;\nfrontend/src/store/channelRefresh.ts:144:                      context.commands.channelMembers(id),\nfrontend/src/store/channelActions.ts:39:    channelMembers(id: string): Promise<ChannelMembersInfo>;\nfrontend/src/store/channelActions.ts:189:          commands.channelMembers(group),\nfrontend/src/store/chat.ts:1925:        const info = await readWithDeadline(() => chat.channelMembers(c.id));\nfrontend/src/features/chat/MembersDialog.tsx:197:    void chatApi.channelMembers(active.id).then(\nfrontend/src/features/chat/ChannelHistorySettings.tsx:84:    void chat.channelMembers(channelId).then(\nsrc-tauri/src/owner_commands.rs:2313:                .channel_members(id)\nsrc-tauri/src/owner_commands.rs:2510:                .channel_members(id)\nsrc-tauri/src/chat_commands/channels.rs:173:pub async fn channel_members(\nsrc-tauri/src/chat_commands/channels.rs:204:                rt.channel_members(channel)\n                    .map(|member| ChannelMemberFact {\n                        public: member.public.clone(),\n                        account_id: member.account_id.clone(),\n                        pending: member.pending,\n                        replica_enabled: false,\n                        reference_name: member.name.clone(),\n                        post_office: member.post_office,\n                    })\n                    .collect()\n            } else {\n                rt.channel_members(channel)\n                    .into_iter()\n                    .map(|public| {\n                        let account = rt.channel_member_account_binding(channel, &public);\n                        let user = public.user_id();\n                        ChannelMemberFact {\n                            post_office: node.device_is_post_office(&public),\n                            public,\n                            account_id: account,\n                            pending: pending.contains(&user),\n                            replica_enabled: rt.channel_replica_enabled(channel, &user),\n                            reference_name: None,\n                        }\n                    })\n                    .collect()\n            };\n            let legacy_membership = reference.as_ref().map_or_else(\n                || node.channel_legacy_membership(channel),\n                |reference| reference.legacy_membership,\n            );\n            let members = display_member_facts(legacy_membership, facts)\n                .into_iter()\n                .map(\n                    |ChannelMemberFact {\n                         public,\n                         account_id,\n                         pending,\n                         replica_enabled,\n                         reference_name,\n                         ..\n                     }| {\n                        let user_id = public.user_id();\n                        let name = if account_id.as_deref() == Some(own_account) {\n                            rt.display_name().to_string()\n                        } else {\n                            account_id\n                                .as_ref()\n                                .and_then(|id| known_names.get(id))\n                                .and_then(|names| names.first())\n                                .cloned()\n                                .or_else(|| {\n                                    (account_id.is_none()\n                                        || rt.account_id_for_device(&public) == account_id)\n                                        .then(|| rt.display_name_for(&user_id))\n                                        .flatten()\n                                })\n                                .or(reference_name)\n                                .unwrap_or_else(|| user_id.clone())\n                        };\n                        ChannelMemberInfo {\n                            file_sharing: (reference.is_none() && user_id == node.user_id())\n                                .then(|| node.group_file_sharing_status()),\n                            user_id,\n                            name,\n                            account_id,\n                            pending,\n                            replica_enabled,\n                        }\n                    },\n                )\n                .collect();\n            Ok(ChannelMembersInfo {\n                history_policy: match reference.as_ref().and_then(|r| r.observed_history_policy()) {\n                    Some(policy) => policy,\n                    None => node.channel_history_policy(channel)?,\n                },\n                history_policy_known: reference\n                    .as_ref()\n                    .is_none_or(|r| r.observed_history_policy().is_some()),\n                directory_reconciling: reference.as_ref().is_some_and(|r| r.directory_reconciling),\n                owner: reference\n                    .as_ref()\n                    .map(|r| r.owner.clone())\n                    .unwrap_or_else(|| rt.channel_owner(channel)),\n                owner_account_id: reference\n                    .as_ref()\n                    .and_then(|r| r.owner_account_id.clone())\n                    .or_else(|| node.channel_owner_account_id(channel)),\n                can_manage: reference.is_none() && node.channel_can_manage(channel)?,\n                account_access: Some(AccountGroupAccessInfo::read(&node, channel)),\n                members,\n            })\n        })\n        .await\n}\n\n#[tauri::command]\npub async fn set_channel_history_policy(\n    app: tauri::State<'_, AppState>,\n        await Promise.all(\n          Array.from(\n            { length: Math.min(MEMBER_CONCURRENCY, wanted.length) },\n            async () => {\n              while (\n                work.current() &&\n                publication === work.publication &&\n                index < wanted.length\n              ) {\n                const id = wanted[index++].channel_id;\n                try {\n                  members.set(\n                    id,\n                    await readWithDeadline(() =>\n                      context.commands.channelMembers(id),\n                    ),\n                  );\n                  if (work.current() && publicationTimer === undefined) {\n                    publicationTimer = setTimeout(() => {\n                      publicationTimer = undefined;\n                      if (work.current()) publish();\n                    }, 50);\n                  }\n                } catch {\n                  failed = true;\n                }\n              }\n            },\n          ),\n        );\n        if (!work.current()) return;\n        if (publicationTimer !== undefined) {\n          clearTimeout(publicationTimer);\n          publicationTimer = undefined;\n        }\n        publish();\n        if (all && !failed) work.nextFallback = now() + FALLBACK_MS;\n        // A failed targeted fetch must also retry through anti-entropy.\n        if (failed)\n          work.nextFallback = Math.min(work.nextFallback, now() + 2000);\n      } catch {\n        // Leave known summaries and members intact; the next fallback retries.\n        work.nextFallback = Math.min(work.nextFallback, now() + 2000);\n      } finally {\n        if (publicationTimer !== undefined) clearTimeout(publicationTimer);\n        work.fullInFlight = false;\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  function request(channelId: string | null = null): Promise<void> {\n    const work = currentRun();\n    if (!work.current()) return Promise.resolve();\n    if (channelId === null || work.dirty.size >= MAX_DIRTY_CHANNELS) {\n      work.all = true;\n      work.dirty.clear();\n    } else if (!work.all) work.dirty.add(channelId);\n    if (!work.promise) start(work);\n    return work.promise!;\n  }\n\n# Module Ownership and Reuse\n\nThis is the implementation ownership map for maintaining Mesh Talk and assigning\nparallel work. Use it to locate the owner of a decision before adding another\nimplementation. Network semantics and configuration belong to the\n[communication architecture](network-design-reference.md); this document defines\nwhere those decisions live in code and how to change them safely.\n\nThe [canonical glossary](../CONTEXT.md) defines domain concepts;\n[DDD conventions](domain-design.md) define modeling terms and identifier mappings.\nThe layers and owners below are implementation responsibilities, not declarations\nthat every module or crate is a separate DDD bounded context.\n\n## 1. Dependency direction\n\n| Layer                                       | Owns                                                                                          | Depends on                                              | Must delegate                                                        |\n| ------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Protocol core: `crates/mesh-talk-core`      | Identity, membership, encryption, admission, persistence, transport and delivery correctness  | Rust libraries and its internal modules                 | Native platform behavior and presentation                            |\n| Desktop host: `src-tauri`                   | Session/runtime installation, OS integration, settings persistence, authorized IPC adaptation | Core public exports                                     | Wire validation, cryptographic authority and delivery state machines |\n| Typed IPC: `frontend/src/lib/api`           | Command names, payload shapes, typed results                                                  | Shared types, Tauri APIs and sibling adapters           | UI stores, React features and business decisions                     |\n| Application stores: `frontend/src/store`    | Reactive state, owner-scoped work, optimistic intents, cache transitions                      | Typed adapters and shared projections                   | Core authority and feature rendering                                 |\n| Feature modules: `frontend/src/features`    | User interaction and composition                                                              | Stores, typed adapters, shared models and UI primitives | Reimplementation of identity, policy or delivery rules               |\n| UI primitives: `frontend/src/components/ui` | Accessible visual controls                                                                    | React/Radix and styling helpers                         | Session lifecycle and protocol policy                                |\n\nThe bot integration service in `crates/mesh-talk-integrations` depends on the core\nand host-supplied admission ports. It owns grants, bounded metadata audit and\nprivate IPC and its fixed-route loopback HTTP adapter; `crates/mesh-talk-mcp` owns SDK/stdio translation only. Core\n`node/outgoing_message.rs` owns retry-safe event acceptance and sender-state WAL\nrecovery. Desktop `src-tauri/src/integrations.rs` binds exact-session leases and\ngraceful listener retirement. `integrations/local_access.rs` owns serialized\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":10625}},"started_at_ms":1795415125536,"completed_at_ms":1795415125537}}
