tform; verify the local member pause/exception control.\nEscalation: Verify native packaged-app foreground/background/tray capture, OS shortcut conflicts and screen-recording permission on macOS, Windows and Linux; browser mocks do not prove native global shortcut registration.\nEscalation: Verify packaged OS prompts and export/link/agent cancellation on each supported platform; test hooks and browser mocks do not certify native credential release.\nEscalation: Verify registered IPC and actual linked-device group footer convergence.\nEscalation: Verify registered main-window presentation IPC, queued hide/ack/fallback ordering and hidden launch. Preserve X11 placement and geometry; require actual packaged first-visible-frame evidence plus browser image/library readiness and unchanged visuals.\nEscalation: Verify switching, clearing, Unicode restoration and inactive previews in browser scenarios. Browser reload with mocked IPC does not certify native quit/restart persistence.\nEscalation: Verify switching, reload persistence, short-window creation and sidebar/settings layout in Portuguese and Korean. Browser mocks cover interface behavior, not native operating-system menus or translated article content.\nEscalation: Visible presence failures require the person-presence browser scenarios, including footer containment, keyboard disclosure and recovery. Native discovery semantics remain owned by the host/core.\nEscalation: Windows execution changes require real windows-process-owner.test.mjs execution on Windows: portable receipt-rejection controls alone do not establish native job membership or retirement. Preserve creation-time job ownership, argument/environment/byte-stream fidelity, cancellation and output/log failure cleanup, helper-death quarantine, unrelated-process isolation and declared-input cache invalidation. Qualify actual cold/cached Cargo test completion, original nonzero status and descendant retirement before subsequent real command admission. Hosted Windows Health remains required before merge. Functional CLI report fixtures await natural closure through the canonical process owner and verify descendant retirement before deleting temporary repositories. Verified forced retirement is an ownership diagnostic; preserve the actual command status and execution error separately. Their sixty-second watchdog prevents deadlock; startup latency is not report acceptance. Preserve passing/failing, empty/blocked, reused, invalidated and rejected-destination assertions, and leave explicit cancellation/deadline controls unchanged.\ndevelopment feedback; mandatory PR/review/CI gates unchanged\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":358040542}},"started_at_ms":1795415183070,"completed_at_ms":1795415184428}}
