{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T06:36:57.230Z","ordinal":38312,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1feaf-24d9-7612-a284-664abd64a2c4","turn_id":"01a2071e-f3c3-7b83-bdd5-c4d356432648","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-58b2c76f-b12c-43c2-a0bc-e27019067342","process_id":"36525","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","cat frontend/src/features/chat/useSerialPoll.ts\nsed -n '1231,1276p' frontend/validation.json\nrg -n 'foreground|recovery' docs/event-driven-design.md | tail -15\ngit status -sb | head -6"],"cwd":"file:///Users/kingsonwu/programming/OctopusGarage/mesh-talk","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"cat frontend/src/features/chat/useSerialPoll.ts\nsed -n '1231,1276p' frontend/validation.json\nrg -n 'foreground|recovery' docs/event-driven-design.md | tail -15\ngit status -sb | head -6"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"import {\n  isNativeWindowMinimized,\n  subscribeNativeWindowMinimized,\n} from \"@/lib/nativeWindowVisibility\";\nimport {\n  subscribeSyncInvalidation,\n  supportsPushState,\n  type SyncInvalidation,\n} from \"@/lib/syncInvalidation\";\nimport { readWithDeadline } from \"@/lib/readDeadline\";\nimport { RECOVERY_REFRESH_MS } from \"@/lib/recoveryRefresh\";\nimport { useEffect, useRef } from \"react\";\n\n/** Event-owned refresh with one visible recovery deadline and one actual read. */\nexport function useSerialPoll<T>(\n  enabled: boolean,\n  intervalMs: number,\n  request: () => Promise<T>,\n  onResult: (result: T) => void,\n  onError: (error: unknown) => void,\n  wakeOn?: SyncInvalidation[\"kind\"],\n  acceptsInvalidation?: (change: SyncInvalidation) => boolean,\n  pushRecoveryMs = RECOVERY_REFRESH_MS,\n) {\n  const handlers = useRef({ request, onResult, onError, acceptsInvalidation });\n  useEffect(() => {\n    handlers.current = { request, onResult, onError, acceptsInvalidation };\n  }, [request, onResult, onError, acceptsInvalidation]);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    if (!enabled) return;\n    let active = true;\n    let busy = false;\n    let dirty = false;\n    let timer: ReturnType<typeof setTimeout> | undefined;\n    const hidden = () => document.hidden || isNativeWindowMinimized();\n    const schedule = () => {\n      clearTimeout(timer);\n      if (!active || busy || hidden()) return;\n      const delay = wakeOn && supportsPushState() ? pushRecoveryMs : intervalMs;\n      timer = setTimeout(() => poll(), delay);\n    };\n    const poll = (invalidate = false) => {\n      if (!active) return;\n      if (busy || hidden()) {\n        dirty ||= invalidate;\n        return;\n      }\n      busy = true;\n      dirty = false;\n      clearTimeout(timer);\n      let physical: Promise<void> | undefined;\n      void readWithDeadline(() => {\n        const operation = Promise.resolve(handlers.current.request());\n        physical = operation.then(\n          () => {},\n          () => {},\n        );\n        return operation;\n      })\n        .then(\n          (result) => {\n            if (active) handlers.current.onResult(result);\n          },\n          (error) => {\n            if (active) handlers.current.onError(error);\n          },\n        )\n        .finally(() => {\n          const release = () => {\n            busy = false;\n            if (!active) return;\n            if (dirty && !hidden()) poll();\n            else schedule();\n          };\n          // A UI timeout cannot cancel native work. Drain after actual settlement\n          // and after the global read admission has released its original slot.\n          if (physical) void physical.then(() => queueMicrotask(release));\n          else release();\n        });\n    };\n    const unlisten = subscribeSyncInvalidation((change) => {\n      if (\n        change.kind === wakeOn &&\n        (handlers.current.acceptsInvalidation?.(change) ?? true)\n      )\n        poll(true);\n    });\n    const foreground = () => {\n      if (!hidden()) poll(true);\n      else clearTimeout(timer);\n    };\n    window.addEventListener(\"focus\", foreground);\n    document.addEventListener(\"visibilitychange\", foreground);\n    const stopNative = subscribeNativeWindowMinimized(foreground);\n    poll();\n    return () => {\n      active = false;\n      clearTimeout(timer);\n      window.removeEventListener(\"focus\", foreground);\n      document.removeEventListener(\"visibilitychange\", foreground);\n      stopNative();\n      unlisten();\n    };\n  }, [enabled, intervalMs, wakeOn, pushRecoveryMs]);\n}\n        \"frontend/src/features/chat/useSerialPoll.ts\",\n        \"frontend/src/features/chat/useSerialPoll.test.ts\",\n        \"frontend/src/features/chat/PersonalDevices.tsx\",\n        \"frontend/src/features/chat/PersonalDevices.test.ts\",\n        \"frontend/e2e/automatic-delivery.spec.ts\",\n        \"frontend/src/lib/api.test.ts\",\n        \"frontend/src/features/chat/LinkDeviceDialog.tsx\",\n        \"frontend/src/features/chat/LinkDeviceDialog.test.ts\",\n        \"frontend/e2e/audit-fixes.spec.ts\",\n        \"frontend/src/lib/i18n.ts\",\n        \"frontend/src/store/privacy.ts\",\n        \"frontend/src/store/privacy.test.ts\",\n        \"frontend/src/lib/recoveryRefresh.ts\",\n        \"frontend/src/lib/recoveryRefresh.test.ts\",\n        \"frontend/src/lib/linkedCustomizationPacks.ts\",\n        \"frontend/src/lib/linkedCustomizationPacks.test.ts\",\n        \"frontend/src/lib/linkedAvatarOverrides.ts\",\n        \"frontend/src/lib/linkedAvatarOverrides.test.ts\",\n        \"frontend/src/lib/linkedReadReceipts.ts\",\n        \"frontend/src/lib/linkedReadReceipts.test.ts\",\n        \"frontend/src/store/drafts.test.ts\"\n      ],\n      \"frontend\": [\n        \"src/lib/readDeadline.test.ts\",\n        \"src/lib/events.test.ts\",\n        \"src/lib/linkedContacts.test.ts\",\n        \"src/lib/linkedAppearance.test.ts\",\n        \"src/lib/linkedPreferencePublisher.test.ts\",\n        \"src/store/fileAvailability.test.ts\",\n        \"src/store/presence.test.ts\",\n        \"src/store/contactPolicy.test.ts\",\n        \"src/features/chat/useSerialPoll.test.ts\",\n        \"src/features/chat/PersonalDevices.test.ts\",\n        \"src/lib/api.test.ts\",\n        \"src/features/chat/LinkDeviceDialog.test.ts\",\n        \"src/store/privacy.test.ts\",\n        \"src/lib/recoveryRefresh.test.ts\",\n        \"src/lib/linkedCustomizationPacks.test.ts\",\n        \"src/lib/linkedAvatarOverrides.test.ts\",\n        \"src/lib/linkedReadReceipts.test.ts\",\n        \"src/store/drafts.test.ts\"\n      ],\n      \"consumers\": [\n        \"frontend-chat\",\n        \"frontend-outgoing\",\n        \"frontend-channel-refresh\",\n33:| Network availability and cost | The platform adapter observes network cost. A change may permit previously blocked work. | Reuse the [native network-cost observer](../src-tauri/src/network_cost/mod.rs). macOS uses native callbacks. Linux and Windows share a serial query owner with event-triggered repair and a sparse fallback. Protocol reconnect, discovery and recovery stay with their existing owners. |\n36:| Window focus, visibility and page exit | The browser reports presentation lifecycle. Foreground is a useful reconciliation trigger. | Use the owning effect's focus and visibility handlers. [Chat](../frontend/src/store/chat.ts) already resumes reception and flushes pending receipt state. [Serial polling](../frontend/src/features/chat/useSerialPoll.ts) offers a scoped refresh with one in-flight read and a visible recovery deadline. Share an adapter when multiple consumers need the same lifecycle and coalescing policy. |\n63:2. Define startup and recovery together. Register before taking the initial\n104:commit timing, authorized consumers, initial read and recovery path. Record\n118:repair component described in [Scheduled work and recovery](scheduled-work.md).\n123:promptly, and failures retain bounded retry and recovery.\n127:See [Scheduled work and recovery](scheduled-work.md) for existing components,\n135:| Repair missed invalidation | Reconcile through the owner's snapshot or cursor on startup, reconnect or foreground. Use a sparse fallback where delivery can be absent or incomplete. Measure necessity before changing it. |\n146:Document its trigger, cadence, actual work, foreground and background scope,\n147:recovery guarantee, and cancellation path. Check whether a reliable producer\n151:as applicable. Keep retry, expiry, heartbeat and recovery controls specific to\n156:share a policy. Measure both normal foreground operation and return to idle,\n165:- Compare foreground handlers in chat, unread badges, notification permissions\n166:  and settings. Share foreground observation only where hide/show handling,\n170:  replacement before changing its recovery cadence.\n## requirements-work...origin/requirements-work [ahead 13]\n M AGENTS.md\n M Cargo.lock\n M crates/mesh-talk-core/Cargo.toml\n M crates/mesh-talk-core/src/discovery/mod.rs\n M crates/mesh-talk-core/src/discovery/roster.rs\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":12833}},"started_at_ms":1795415817230,"completed_at_ms":1795415817230}}
