{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T06:40:45.081Z","ordinal":38476,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1feaf-24d9-7612-a284-664abd64a2c4","turn_id":"01a20722-1e9f-7062-b0ab-0ca7026be9e3","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-8531540c-72aa-4553-bdda-046fad6388ad","process_id":"3980","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '10,34p' docs/performance-requirements.md\nls tmp/req-011 | rg 'audit|ledger|evidence.*json|score|matrix|status' | head -20\ngit diff --check\ndate +%s"],"cwd":"file:///Users/kingsonwu/programming/OctopusGarage/mesh-talk","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"sed -n '10,34p' docs/performance-requirements.md\nls tmp/req-011 | rg 'audit|ledger|evidence.*json|score|matrix|status' | head -20\ngit diff --check\ndate +%s"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"\nThese are initial project targets, **not industry standards or claims that the\ncurrent application meets them**. Establish a production-build baseline on each\nsupported platform. Reference fixture: 4 logical CPUs, 8 GiB RAM, SSD, 100 contacts,\n20 groups and 100,000 stored messages; no pending transfers, calls or animations.\nSeparate cold start, warm start, catch-up, visible idle and hidden idle. Measure a\nquiet five-minute window after warmup; record build, runtime, profile and workload.\nWarm startup restarts the process with OS caches retained; cold startup records\nits uncached/first-launch conditions. Usable means an actionable list or\nconversation, not a blank shell; report human authorization waits separately.\nThe empty-shell comparison keeps the same backend, runtime, process membership\nand window settings, with user payloads absent.\n\n| Resource                | Initial target for the reference fixture                                                                                                                                                            |\n| ----------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Idle CPU                | Visible desktop: ≤1% of one logical CPU; hidden desktop: ≤0.25%; headless node: ≤0.5%, averaged over the window.                                                                                    |\n| Retained memory         | Headless node: ≤64 MiB private commit. Desktop: ≤64 MiB workload delta above the same-build empty shell; establish a reviewed whole-family ceiling from that baseline.                              |\n| Memory growth           | Repeated navigation/media cycles reach a bounded plateau. Tenfold stored history must not require tenfold startup reads or retained UI payloads.                                                    |\n| Idle writes             | Zero business-data commits for unchanged inputs. Target ≤5 MiB/hour OS-observed attributable storage writes per application family after warmup; measure the full hour before claiming this target. |\n| Background wakeups      | No application maintenance timer without pending work, a real deadline or a documented recovery purpose. Noncritical recovery defaults to ≥5 minutes and coalesces activation.                      |\n| Startup and interaction | First usable shell ≤1 s warm / ≤3 s cold; ordinary interaction must not run blocking I/O, crypto or an unbounded traversal on the UI thread. Report hydration/catch-up separately.                  |\n\nCPU means `100 × process CPU seconds / wall seconds`, summed over the full app\nfamily; divide by logical CPU count only when reporting whole-machine percent.\nReport Rust host **and** renderer/GPU/helpers. Distinguish private commit, private\noutgoing-status-batch-tests.log\noutgoing-status-batch-typecheck.log\noutgoing-status-reference-red.log\noutgoing-status-reference-tests.log\noutgoing-status-reference-typecheck.log\n1795416045\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":10834}},"started_at_ms":1795416045081,"completed_at_ms":1795416045081}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T06:40:45.152Z","ordinal":38477,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a20722-b660-7042-9003-bf04e096adc5","call_id":"call_e14ea43fb934428fabe43ed69074a7b5","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.3 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"b9aa92\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000010834,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":778,\"output\":\"\\nThese are initial project targets, **not industry standards or claims that the\\ncurrent application meets them**. Establish a production-build baseline on each\\nsupported platform. Reference fixture: 4 logical CPUs, 8 GiB RAM, SSD, 100 contacts,\\n20 groups and 100,000 stored messages; no pending transfers, calls or animations.\\nSeparate cold start, warm start, catch-up, visible idle and hidden idle. Measure a\\nquiet five-minute window after warmup; record build, runtime, profile and workload.\\nWarm startup restarts the process with OS caches retained; cold startup records\\nits uncached/first-launch conditions. Usable means an actionable list or\\nconversation, not a blank shell; report human authorization waits separately.\\nThe empty-shell comparison keeps the same backend, runtime, process membership\\nand window settings, with user payloads absent.\\n\\n| Resource                | Initial target for the reference fixture                                                                                                                                                            |\\n| ----------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\\n| Idle CPU                | Visible desktop: ≤1% of one logical CPU; hidden desktop: ≤0.25%; headless node: ≤0.5%, averaged over the window.                                                                                    |\\n| Retained memory         | Headless node: ≤64 MiB private commit. Desktop: ≤64 MiB workload delta above the same-build empty shell; establish a reviewed whole-family ceiling from that baseline.                              |\\n| Memory growth           | Repeated navigation/media cycles reach a bounded plateau. Tenfold stored history must not require tenfold startup reads or retained UI payloads.                                                    |\\n| Idle writes             | Zero business-data commits for unchanged inputs. Target ≤5 MiB/hour OS-observed attributable storage writes per application family after warmup; measure the full hour before claiming this target. |\\n| Background wakeups      | No application maintenance timer without pending work, a real deadline or a documented recovery purpose. Noncritical recovery defaults to ≥5 minutes and coalesces activation.                      |\\n| Startup and interaction | First usable shell ≤1 s warm / ≤3 s cold; ordinary interaction must not run blocking I/O, crypto or an unbounded traversal on the UI thread. Report hydration/catch-up separately.                  |\\n\\nCPU means `100 × process CPU seconds / wall seconds`, summed over the full app\\nfamily; divide by logical CPU count only when reporting whole-machine percent.\\nReport Rust host **and** renderer/GPU/helpers. Distinguish private commit, private\\noutgoing-status-batch-tests.log\\noutgoing-status-batch-typecheck.log\\noutgoing-status-reference-red.log\\noutgoing-status-reference-tests.log\\noutgoing-status-reference-typecheck.log\\n1795416045\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a20722-1e9f-7062-b0ab-0ca7026be9e3","create_time":1795416045.152826}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":16328,"sampled_through_sequence":16325,"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000,"model_search_state":"unused"}}
