{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T07:41:11.668Z","ordinal":40451,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1feaf-24d9-7612-a284-664abd64a2c4","turn_id":"01a20756-9c6d-7151-b9aa-d3f86228c963","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-0e9a4983-3c9a-4a7a-a91d-716140557198","process_id":"46705","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","cat tmp/requirements-order.md | rg -n 'REQ-0(12|13|19|22|25|26|27|28|29|30)|parallel' ; sed -n '813,842p;898,938p;968,996p' /Users/kingsonwu/.t3/userdata/attachments/9fbeff35-b275-4d28-827e-0793705b1548-3e613045-3824-44c2-9b76-5f5a3edca4d2-md.md; git diff --name-only | rg -i 'privacy|block|trust|docs/' | head -30"],"cwd":"file:///Users/kingsonwu/programming/OctopusGarage/mesh-talk","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"cat tmp/requirements-order.md | rg -n 'REQ-0(12|13|19|22|25|26|27|28|29|30)|parallel' ; sed -n '813,842p;898,938p;968,996p' /Users/kingsonwu/.t3/userdata/attachments/9fbeff35-b275-4d28-827e-0793705b1548-3e613045-3824-44c2-9b76-5f5a3edca4d2-md.md; git diff --name-only | rg -i 'privacy|block|trust|docs/' | head -30"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"13:4. Address REQ-004, REQ-009, REQ-022 and REQ-030 within the change that needs\n15:5. Use measurements to scope REQ-007 and REQ-012. Apply REQ-013 and REQ-018\n20:   checks. Define REQ-019 propagation and retention before REQ-024 forwarding.\n21:   REQ-026 has its own audience rules. Use REQ-025 before allowing stranger\n22:   contact, validate REQ-027 pairing and browser feasibility before expansion,\n23:   and defer REQ-028 until optional resources need allocation. Apply REQ-029\n### REQ-022 — Preserve decision rationale and reasons for not implementing alternatives\n\n- **Discussion state:** Confirmed at scope/principle level; detailed recording conventions and enforcement remain undecided.\n- **Captured / updated:** 2026-11-17 (Asia/Singapore).\n- **Original user input:** “建立这样一种文档机制，用于后续引导AI等：记录一些为什么不实现之类的记录，避免以后忘记又要想实现 / 以及一些方案选择的原因，避免以后忘记又要想改 / 等等”。\n- **Scenario and affected users:** Future AI/developer sessions revisit features and architecture without the original discussion context, potentially repeating rejected work or undoing intentional choices.\n- **Pain point or question:** Preserve why a feature was not implemented or an approach was chosen, so later work does not reopen decisions simply because the rationale was forgotten. Specific missing decisions or current document gaps not audited.\n- **Desired outcome:** Discoverable, maintained decision records that explain choices, non-goals and deferred/rejected alternatives and guide future proposals using their current assumptions and evidence.\n- **Confirmed scope from user:** A documentation mechanism for AI and other maintainers recording reasons not to implement ideas and reasons for selected approaches, reducing repeated reconsideration caused by lost context.\n- **Additional user-confirmed principles:** Record reasons, explicit status and reconsideration conditions; prefer existing topic guides; use ADRs for significant trade-offs; guide AI to consult relevant records before proposing changes. Continue intake without investigation or implementation.\n- **Additional original user confirmation:** “符合我的意思。REQ-022 采用‘记录理由＋明确状态＋重新评估条件’，优先复用已有主题文档，重要取舍使用 ADR，并引导 AI 在提出相关改动前查阅。请更新为范围已确认，继续收集需求，暂不调查或实施。”\n- **Assistant-proposed recording details — unconfirmed:**\n  - Record the question, affected capability/owner, decision/status/date, constraints and evidence, considered alternatives, chosen approach and why others were not adopted, consequences and links to relevant contracts/code/tests/PRs.\n  - Distinguish not implemented yet, explicitly deferred, rejected under current constraints, and out of product scope. Missing implementation alone is not evidence of deliberate rejection.\n  - Include reconsideration conditions: changed requirements, new evidence, removed constraints or relevant technology/security changes. Records preserve reasoning, not an eternal prohibition on changing course.\n  - Identify current versus superseded decisions and link replacements. Keep history/traceability without maintaining conflicting active rules; never invent the historical rationale when it is unknown.\n  - Only user/owner-confirmed choices are decisions; label assistant proposals and unverified interpretations accordingly.\n- **Assistant-proposed document ownership and AI use — unconfirmed:**\n  - Reuse existing maintained topic guides and documented ADR conventions after later inspection. A short rationale may live beside its owning contract; significant difficult-to-reverse trade-offs may warrant a linked ADR. Do not create an ADR for every small edit or a second competing rulebook.\n  - Provide a discoverable index/navigation and topic links so future AI sessions consult relevant decisions before proposing implementation, replacement or refactoring. Link from maintained AI guidance to the owners rather than copy all rationales into every prompt.\n  - When revisiting a decision, cite the original reason, identify what assumption/evidence changed and propose an explicit reviewed update rather than silently reversing it. Current user direction and confirmed changed requirements can supersede prior decisions; old text is not an automatic veto.\n  - Keep temporary investigation logs, chat transcripts and completed-work diaries out of maintained decision guidance. Update concise durable reasoning instead of accumulating uncurated notes.\n  - Any automated structural check should have a justified low-cost role; text presence does not prove decision quality. No new CI gate or external-memory system selected.\n- **Candidate acceptance evidence — unconfirmed:** Relevant decisions can be located through maintained navigation; a representative feature rejection and architectural choice include rationale/status/revisit conditions; an AI workflow can discover and apply them without silently treating a deferred idea as prohibited. Existing conflicting guidance reconciled. Detailed templates and thresholds remain open.\n- **Open questions:**\n  1. What significance threshold and document owner should determine where each rationale lives? Inspect existing conventions later before adding files or duplicate processes.\n  2. Which existing decisions need backfilling, and what source evidence supports their rationale? Unknown historical reasoning must remain marked unknown until verified. These details do not block continued collection.\n- **Related records and evidence:** REQ-009 maintained technical docs; REQ-004 domain/ownership; REQ-005/011 AI programming guidance; REQ-007/012/018/020/021 future choices needing explicit reasoning. These links do not set order/dependencies. No decision-policy implementation, ADR creation, historical audit or AI rules changed during intake.\n- **Global planning:** Classification, priority, effort, dependency analysis, roadmap phase and branch allocation deferred until collection closes. Current work only records and clarifies requirements.\n\n### REQ-025 — Configurable anti-harassment, blocking and trust endorsements\n\n- **Discussion state:** Clarifying; public-network protection and trust ideas captured, enforcement and scoring rules unselected.\n- **Captured / updated:** 2026-11-17 (Asia/Singapore).\n- **Original user input:** “认证和防骚扰机制，这样如果去外面的比如接入星巴克之类的网络，可以根据自己设置的选择，防止被骚扰之类的：防骚扰机制，支持屏蔽设备？屏蔽账号，还是啥。账号能不能增加认证数，经过哪些你认证过的人认证之类的？增加可信度。便于后续做防骚扰机制？？”\n- **Scenario and affected users:** Users joining shared/public networks, such as a café Wi-Fi, want control over unsolicited contact and a useful indication of trust without assuming everyone on the LAN is trusted.\n- **Pain point or question:** Which identities/actions should be blocked or filtered, and could endorsements by already trusted contacts help assess another account? No existing block/contact/verification mechanism audited and no actual abuse incident established.\n- **Desired outcome:** User-configurable anti-harassment behavior with clear identity/permission boundaries; investigate trustworthy, privacy-aware endorsements as an optional input rather than assume a count proves safety.\n- **Confirmed topic scope from user:** Public-network protection; user-selected policies; explore device/account blocking; explore account certification/endorsement counts and who among trusted/verified contacts endorses someone. No identity proof, web-of-trust algorithm or automatic admission rule selected.\n- **Assistant-proposed protection boundaries — unconfirmed:**\n  - Distinguish cryptographic account/device authentication, an explicit human verification/endorsement, personal trust and authorization to contact. A valid key proves a different fact from being a trusted person; a numeric endorsement count is not a safety guarantee.\n  - Evaluate account-level blocking with device-level controls as appropriate; define effects across the account's existing/new devices, linked local devices, group interactions and integrations. An IP address is not assumed to be stable account identity or the sole block key.\n  - Clarify contact requests/message quarantine, notification filtering, call/file invitations, group/forum traffic and connection/resource admission separately. Hiding UI alone may not prevent unwanted background work; blocking a sender must also preserve legitimate shared-group/protocol behavior under a defined contract.\n  - Candidate public-network modes could restrict unsolicited interaction to trusted contacts, queue requests or allow chosen categories. No automatic network-name-based trust, default mode or no-discovery behavior selected.\n- **Assistant-proposed endorsement questions — unconfirmed:**\n  - What a statement attests to (person/key verified, prior interaction or recommendation), who issued it, scope, provenance, revocation and expiry must be explicit. Do not assume endorsement is transitive or an endorsement grants contact permission.\n  - Distinguish endorsements from people the user directly trusts from total global counts. Evaluate fabricated/multiple-account endorsements, collusion, stale/offline revocations and resource-limited verification before choosing scoring/thresholds.\n  - Define private versus published trust relationships and whether displaying names/counts leaks a social graph. Do not expose contacts or endorsements by default solely to build a score.\n  - Evaluate reasonable controls for new/unknown users and compromised/revoked trusted identities; do not require a universal centralized identity/certification service from the word authentication.\n- **Candidate acceptance evidence — unconfirmed:** Explicit configurable stranger-contact/block behavior; correct account/device and linked-device scope; no automatic call/file acceptance or unexpected contact privilege from a score; effective revoke/unblock/expiry behavior for selected features; bounded spam/resource handling; documented limits against key rotation/new accounts and privacy leakage. Concrete defaults, thresholds and protocols remain open.\n- **Open questions:**\n  1. For public-network use, should the primary policy restrict unknown users to a contact-request queue rather than direct messages/calls, with an optional trusted-contacts-only mode? Assistant recommendation: discuss configurable stranger-contact behavior first; endorsement scoring can remain exploratory.\n  2. Should blocking primarily target an account across its devices, with device blocking as an additional control? Verify existing identity/contracts later before implementation.\n  3. What does an endorsement mean, who can see it and how may it affect access? No score/threshold selected; keep separate from verified identity and permission.\n- **Related records and evidence:** REQ-013 privacy/tracking, REQ-004 identity terminology, REQ-018 membership/authenticated propagation, REQ-019/024 forum audience/abuse and REQ-021 client access contracts. The same user message separately updates forum retention in REQ-024. No external security research, code audit, block policy or trust implementation performed.\n- **Global planning:** Classification, priority, effort, dependency analysis, roadmap phase and branch allocation deferred until collection closes. Current work records and clarifies only.\n\n### REQ-026 — Personal feed, profile and sharing exploration\n\n- **Discussion state:** Clarifying; per-post audience control and independent profile visibility confirmed, propagation and detailed policies remain open.\n- **Captured / updated:** 2026-11-17 (Asia/Singapore).\n- **Original user input:** “REQ-026 先作为朋友圈、个人主页与分享的探索方向记录，不预设公开范围或传播机制；请区分它与论坛的使用场景，先澄清面向哪些人可见，一次问一个关键问题。继续收集需求，暂不调查或实施。”\n- **Scenario and affected users:** Explore a person-centered feed, personal profile/homepage and sharing experience. Each post targets contacts selected by its publisher; profile visibility is separately configured. Relationship semantics and detailed controls remain open.\n- **Desired outcome:** Clarify who the personal content is for and how this differs from forum discussion before selecting publication or synchronization rules.\n- **Confirmed boundaries:** Each post lets its publisher choose visible contacts; sharing is not public by default. Personal profile/homepage visibility is configured independently. Propagation mechanisms remain open. Ask one key question at a time. Do not investigate or implement now.\n- **Additional original user clarification:** “REQ-026 先支持发布者逐条选择可见联系人，不默认公开；个人主页的可见范围单独配置，传播机制继续待讨论。请更新文档，再一次澄清一个 REQ-027 的关键边界，继续收集需求，暂不调查或实施。”\n- **Assistant-proposed distinction — unconfirmed:** A personal feed/profile can center on a person and their selected audience, while REQ-019 forum exploration can center on topics/community discussion. This is a discussion aid, not a chosen product model; do not merge them automatically or assume mutual-contact relationships already exist.\n- **Deferred questions:** Profile audience options, editing an existing post's audience, forwarding/replies and enforceable propagation/access-revocation behavior remain to clarify later. Per-post selected contacts and independent profile controls do not grant a recipient permission to redistribute. Discuss these later one at a time; the prior request to move on to REQ-027 did not resolve them.\n- **Candidate evidence / related items:** Later define a concrete author/viewer sharing flow and access boundary. REQ-019 forum, REQ-024 forwarding, REQ-025 trust/harassment and REQ-013 privacy are context. Forum three-day expiry is not automatically a policy for personal posts. No propagation, retention, interaction or identity feature selected.\n- **Global planning:** Classification, priority, effort, dependencies, roadmap and branch decisions deferred until collection closes. Current work records and clarifies only.\n\n### REQ-028 — Explore contribution incentives, reputation and tamper-resistant resource priority\n\n- **Discussion state:** Clarifying; explicitly exploratory extension, not an approved scoring or admission system.\n- **Captured / updated:** 2026-11-17 (Asia/Singapore).\n- **Original user input:** “积分和信誉机制，放篡改，经常共享的人，或者开启共享的人优先获得从别人那里获取共享消息的优先级；其实就是数据安全，防篡改，以及乐于转发分享的人，优先获得更好的通信质量，其实就是p2p的逻辑”。 Interpret “放篡改” in context as tamper resistance.\n- **Scenario and affected users:** Participants contribute permitted sharing/relay/storage resources and may receive preferential access to others' offered resources, especially under contention.\n- **Pain point or question:** Encourage useful cooperation without corruptible contribution claims, while maintaining data integrity and decentralized operation. Current resource-allocation mechanisms, crypto protections and exploitable gaps have not been inspected.\n- **Desired outcome:** Explore measurable contribution-based incentives and defensible resource allocation, separately from content authenticity and contact trust.\n- **Confirmed scope from user:** Points/reputation, tamper resistance/data security, contribution through enabling sharing and/or actual forwarding, and potentially improved shared-message access priority or communication quality. No currency/blockchain, consensus algorithm, global leaderboard or purchased access selected.\n- **Additional user-confirmed resource scope:** Limit contribution-based priority to optional shared resources such as forum content, files and cache forwarding. Preserve normal basic-chat service. Points algorithms, contribution proofs and anti-gaming mechanisms remain research questions. Continue intake without investigation or implementation.\n- **Additional original user clarification:** “REQ-028 先将贡献优先级限定于论坛、文件和缓存转发等可选共享资源，保障基础聊天正常服务；积分算法、贡献证明和防刷机制保留为待研究项。请更新文档，继续收集需求，暂不调查或实施。”\n- **Assistant-proposed model alternatives — unconfirmed:**\n  - Direct peer reciprocity based on locally observed useful work; scoped signed contribution/receipt records; or broader reputation aggregation. Evaluate complexity, trust, offline behavior, gaming, privacy and overhead before choosing. No global ledger or universally agreed score assumed.\n  - Distinguish willingness to share, resource availability, actual valid delivered/stored work and user-valued content. Enabling a setting, self-reported bytes and peers agreeing to exchange receipts are different evidence; none automatically proves useful contribution.\n  - Distinguish content authenticity/integrity, score-record integrity, truthful contribution evidence, personal trust and access permission. Signed false or collusive claims can remain false; a contribution score must not replace permission or encryption checks.\n- **Assistant-proposed policy boundaries — unconfirmed:**\n  - Define identity/account versus device scope, which peer/community evaluates a score, provenance, age/decay, accounting limits and appeal/reset/recovery as needed. Avoid exposing contact graphs or detailed traffic history simply to make contributions public.\n  - Evaluate fabricated identities, collusion/self-traffic, duplicate/replayed receipts, invalid content, strategic disconnects and compromised keys. Prevent rewarding wasteful replication or unauthorized forwarding; counting traffic can conflict with low-power goals if poorly designed.\n  - Determine eligible traffic and resources: optional forum/cache/file distribution, offline custody and core chat/control traffic have different latency and correctness obligations. Priority is a proposed scheduling benefit, not guaranteed bandwidth on an unavailable/untrusted network.\n  - Consider minimum service, bounded preference, fairness/anti-starvation and new/mobile/resource-constrained participants. No denial/degradation of essential messaging to low-score users selected; do not presume every node must share permanently.\n  - Reuse existing validated crypto, bounded scheduling and metadata rather than introduce continuous proofs, polling or unbounded contribution logs without measured value.\n- **Candidate acceptance evidence — unconfirmed:** Clear contribution/policy contract; evidence provenance and replay/deduplication rules; bounded metadata/CPU/network cost; representative contention fairness and useful-work tests; adversarial fabricated/collusive evidence cases for the selected threat model; no access-control bypass. Define what cannot be verified and avoid claiming perfect anti-fraud or guaranteed quality.\n- **Open questions:**\n  1. Which bounded benefits for optional forum/file/cache sharing are useful without undermining normal basic-chat service? Concrete scheduling/quotas remain open; basic chat must not be differentiated by contribution score under the confirmed scope.\n  2. Is contribution evaluated from local direct experience or intended as portable reputation across communities? No global score requirement selected.\n  3. What useful work deserves credit, and what evidence/cost is acceptable? Decide after concrete scenarios, not a scoring formula first.\n- **Related records and evidence:** REQ-025 identity/endorsement trust is distinct from service contribution; REQ-019/024 content sharing, REQ-018 transport/sync, REQ-013 privacy, REQ-011 low resource use and REQ-015 custody/resource ownership are context. No execution order/dependency graph chosen. No scoring, cryptographic design, protocol research or implementation performed.\n- **Global planning:** Classification, priority, effort, dependency analysis, roadmap phase and branch allocation deferred until collection closes. Current work records and clarifies only.\n\ncrates/mesh-talk-core/src/node/privacy_routes.rs\ncrates/mesh-talk-core/src/node/privacy_routing.rs\ncrates/mesh-talk-core/src/node/privacy_runtime.rs\ndocs/ARCHITECTURE.md\ndocs/backup-recovery.md\ndocs/event-driven-design.md\ndocs/network-design-reference.md\ndocs/performance-requirements.md\ndocs/post-office-federation.md\ndocs/routed-network-discovery.md\ndocs/scheduled-work.md\ndocs/settings.md\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":12042}},"started_at_ms":1795419671667,"completed_at_ms":1795419671668}}
