{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T07:41:19.993Z","ordinal":40457,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0dca4931a04d8132016b03ee1e340887d0badb35c626efbefa","status":"completed","call_id":"call_7c0351f92154403c94d17e119f54ed14","name":"exec","input":"await Promise.allSettled([tools.mcp__english_pilot__english_coaching_context({}),tools.exec_command({cmd:`rg --files docs | rg -i 'adr|decision|documentation'; git branch --show-current; git rev-parse --short HEAD; git worktree list; sed -n '8,25p' tmp/requirements-order.md`,max_output_tokens:1300})]).then(x=>x.forEach(text))\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a20756-9c6d-7151-b9aa-d3f86228c963","create_time":1795419678.2073505}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":17151,"sampled_through_sequence":17149,"client_authored":false,"model_search_state":"unused"}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T07:41:20.286Z","ordinal":40458,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a1feaf-24d9-7612-a284-664abd64a2c4","turn_id":"01a20756-9c6d-7151-b9aa-d3f86228c963","session_id":"01a1feaf-24d9-7612-a284-664abd64a2c4","root_turn_id":"01a20756-9c6d-7151-b9aa-d3f86228c963","response_id":"resp_0dca4931a04d8132016b03ee1a28e887d09c04b39878bb793f","usage":{"input_tokens":387875,"cached_input_tokens":384384,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":128,"reasoning_output_tokens":25,"total_tokens":388003},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":4979638,"cached_input_tokens":4969088,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1825,"reasoning_output_tokens":577,"total_tokens":4981463},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":1461474828,"cached_input_tokens":1455566080,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1265209,"reasoning_output_tokens":325438,"total_tokens":1462740037}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T07:41:21.037Z","ordinal":40459,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1feaf-24d9-7612-a284-664abd64a2c4","turn_id":"01a20756-9c6d-7151-b9aa-d3f86228c963","item":{"type":"McpToolCall","id":"exec-606f75b9-5c97-4a53-8315-077c3cee4dcb","server":"english-pilot","tool":"english_coaching_context","arguments":{},"status":"completed","result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"guidance\": \"Do not derail the user's main task. Enforce mode is enabled: over-threshold prompts are handled by the submit hook before the agent turn. Force mode is enabled: append one English note using the configured note depth whenever the prompt has Chinese fragments, non-native phrasing, or a clearly better everyday expression. Prefer practical workplace English, brief teaching rationale, and reusable expressions.\",\n  \"finalResponseInstruction\": \"Finish the main task first. For the latest allowed user prompt, append one English note using the configured note depth if it contains any Chinese fragment, awkward English, or obvious phrasing improvement: Use a Rich English Note by default: 5-8 useful lines, brief enough for a final response but rich enough for study.\\nUse this shape:\\nEnglish note:\\nOriginal: \\\"fix this problem\\\"\\nBetter: \\\"fix this issue\\\" / \\\"resolve this startup issue\\\"\\nWhy: In engineering conversations, \\\"issue\\\" is more precise than \\\"problem\\\" when discussing bugs, failures, tickets, or startup errors.\\nUseful patterns:\\n- \\\"The MCP client failed during the startup handshake.\\\"\\n- \\\"This issue belongs at the config boundary, not the runtime path.\\\"\\nCollocations: startup issue, handshake failure, config mismatch, reproduce the issue, verify the fix\\nCommon mistake: Use \\\"problem\\\" for general trouble; use \\\"issue\\\" for bugs, tickets, incidents, and engineering discussions.\\nIPA: issue /ˈɪʃuː/ or /ˈɪsjuː/ For programming-task conversations, prefer software-engineering English in the final note. Good sentence patterns: append an English note at the end; keep the behavior behind a small interface; make the failure path explicit; cache the result to avoid repeating the same expensive operation; this change belongs at the module boundary. Use the configured computer-English files as vocabulary hints, not as text to quote every time.\",\n  \"domainReference\": {\n    \"style\": \"software-engineering\",\n    \"available\": false,\n    \"terms\": [],\n    \"examples\": [\n      \"append an English note at the end\",\n      \"keep the behavior behind a small interface\",\n      \"make the failure path explicit\",\n      \"cache the result to avoid repeating the same expensive operation\",\n      \"this change belongs at the module boundary\"\n    ],\n    \"missingPaths\": []\n  },\n  \"cadence\": \"Force mode bypasses cooldown and daily-cap intent for teachable user prompts; follow the configured note depth and keep the note professional. Skip only when there is no meaningful wording improvement.\",\n  \"policy\": {\n    \"gateMode\": \"enforce\",\n    \"intensity\": \"force\",\n    \"cooldownMinutes\": 0,\n    \"maxInlineCoachingPerDay\": 999,\n    \"assistantEnglishNoteDepth\": \"rich\"\n  },\n  \"today\": {\n    \"date\": \"2026-11-23\",\n    \"coachingShown\": 0,\n    \"remaining\": 999\n  },\n  \"cooldown\": {\n    \"active\": false,\n    \"lastShownAt\": \"2026-08-01T13:52:28.084Z\"\n  },\n  \"decision\": {\n    \"shouldOfferInlineCoaching\": true,\n    \"reason\": \"available\"\n  }\n}"}]},"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":38958167}},"started_at_ms":1795419679998,"completed_at_ms":1795419681037}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T07:41:21.381Z","ordinal":40460,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1feaf-24d9-7612-a284-664abd64a2c4","turn_id":"01a20756-9c6d-7151-b9aa-d3f86228c963","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-632ee1ee-2043-43d0-82fb-7d6b95c1c14a","process_id":"84520","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","rg --files docs | rg -i 'adr|decision|documentation'; git branch --show-current; git rev-parse --short HEAD; git worktree list; sed -n '8,25p' tmp/requirements-order.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/kingsonwu/programming/OctopusGarage/mesh-talk","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rg --files docs | rg -i 'adr|decision|documentation'; git branch --show-current; git rev-parse --short HEAD; git worktree list; sed -n '8,25p' tmp/requirements-order.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"docs/DOCUMENTATION_GUIDELINES.md\nrequirements-work\n0ae1a692\n/Users/kingsonwu/programming/OctopusGarage/mesh-talk                                                                                         0ae1a692 [requirements-work]\n/Users/kingsonwu/.ao/data/worktrees/mesh-talk/orchestrator/mesh-talk-orchestrator                                                            d6c1fb6f [ao/mesh-talk-orchestrator]\n/Users/kingsonwu/programming/OctopusGarage/mesh-talk/.worktrees/account-group-unification                                                    dcec05c2 [fix/account-group-unification]\n/Users/kingsonwu/programming/OctopusGarage/mesh-talk/.worktrees/account-group-unification/tmp/account-group-permissions/cooldown-source      032c7eab (detached HEAD)\n/Users/kingsonwu/programming/OctopusGarage/mesh-talk/.worktrees/account-group-unification/tmp/account-group-permissions/dm-receipt-worktree  34283d75 (detached HEAD)\n/Users/kingsonwu/programming/OctopusGarage/mesh-talk/.worktrees/device-trust                                                                 25c9a540 [fix/multi-device-verification]\n/Users/kingsonwu/programming/OctopusGarage/mesh-talk/.worktrees/fix-group-file-relay                                                         ee5a2a41 [fix/group-file-relay]\n/Users/kingsonwu/programming/OctopusGarage/mesh-talk/.worktrees/history-search-pagination                                                    e83bcea5 [feat/history-search-pagination]\n/Users/kingsonwu/programming/OctopusGarage/mesh-talk/.worktrees/optimization-batch-20261013                                                  5f4805f6 (detached HEAD)\n/Users/kingsonwu/programming/OctopusGarage/mesh-talk/.worktrees/optimization-sequence-20261015                                               98c0ff3b [perf/optimization-sequence-20261015]\n/Users/kingsonwu/programming/OctopusGarage/mesh-talk/.worktrees/queued-owner-diagnostics-20261102                                            b11b319e [diagnostics/ci-file-source-20261103]\n/Users/kingsonwu/programming/OctopusGarage/mesh-talk/.worktrees/req-029                                                                      0ae1a692 [req-029]\n/Users/kingsonwu/programming/OctopusGarage/mesh-talk/.worktrees/system-evolution-20261019                                                    1050a83f [feat/system-evolution-20261019]\n2. Follow evidence into REQ-017 (history and memory lifecycle), REQ-006\n   (redundant processing and I/O), or REQ-005 (scheduling). Add the corresponding\n   REQ-011 regression check. Build REQ-001 around verified metrics where useful.\n3. REQ-010 is the first independent feature and the fallback if the initial\n   profile yields no actionable hotspot. REQ-014 and REQ-003 are also independent.\n4. Address REQ-004, REQ-009, REQ-022 and REQ-030 within the change that needs\n   their terminology, documentation, rationale, or verification.\n5. Use measurements to scope REQ-007 and REQ-012. Apply REQ-013 and REQ-018\n   where a feature needs privacy or identity and permission guarantees.\n6. Let actual consumers drive REQ-008 and REQ-015, then REQ-020 and REQ-021\n   when an external consumer or second client has concrete requirements.\n7. REQ-002 and REQ-023 can start independently after their own permission\n   checks. Define REQ-019 propagation and retention before REQ-024 forwarding.\n   REQ-026 has its own audience rules. Use REQ-025 before allowing stranger\n   contact, validate REQ-027 pairing and browser feasibility before expansion,\n   and defer REQ-028 until optional resources need allocation. Apply REQ-029\n   to specific product decisions.\n\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":12375}},"started_at_ms":1795419681381,"completed_at_ms":1795419681381}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T07:41:21.484Z","ordinal":40461,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a2075a-32cc-7db2-b198-ecfe1a6fa715","call_id":"call_7c0351f92154403c94d17e119f54ed14","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.5 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"{\\n  \\\"guidance\\\": \\\"Do not derail the user's main task. Enforce mode is enabled: over-threshold prompts are handled by the submit hook before the agent turn. Force mode is enabled: append one English note using the configured note depth whenever the prompt has Chinese fragments, non-native phrasing, or a clearly better everyday expression. Prefer practical workplace English, brief teaching rationale, and reusable expressions.\\\",\\n  \\\"finalResponseInstruction\\\": \\\"Finish the main task first. For the latest allowed user prompt, append one English note using the configured note depth if it contains any Chinese fragment, awkward English, or obvious phrasing improvement: Use a Rich English Note by default: 5-8 useful lines, brief enough for a final response but rich enough for study.\\\\nUse this shape:\\\\nEnglish note:\\\\nOriginal: \\\\\\\"fix this problem\\\\\\\"\\\\nBetter: \\\\\\\"fix this issue\\\\\\\" / \\\\\\\"resolve this startup issue\\\\\\\"\\\\nWhy: In engineering conversations, \\\\\\\"issue\\\\\\\" is more precise than \\\\\\\"problem\\\\\\\" when discussing bugs, failures, tickets, or startup errors.\\\\nUseful patterns:\\\\n- \\\\\\\"The MCP client failed during the startup handshake.\\\\\\\"\\\\n- \\\\\\\"This issue belongs at the config boundary, not the runtime path.\\\\\\\"\\\\nCollocations: startup issue, handshake failure, config mismatch, reproduce the issue, verify the fix\\\\nCommon mistake: Use \\\\\\\"problem\\\\\\\" for general trouble; use \\\\\\\"issue\\\\\\\" for bugs, tickets, incidents, and engineering discussions.\\\\nIPA: issue /ˈɪʃuː/ or /ˈɪsjuː/ For programming-task conversations, prefer software-engineering English in the final note. Good sentence patterns: append an English note at the end; keep the behavior behind a small interface; make the failure path explicit; cache the result to avoid repeating the same expensive operation; this change belongs at the module boundary. Use the configured computer-English files as vocabulary hints, not as text to quote every time.\\\",\\n  \\\"domainReference\\\": {\\n    \\\"style\\\": \\\"software-engineering\\\",\\n    \\\"available\\\": false,\\n    \\\"terms\\\": [],\\n    \\\"examples\\\": [\\n      \\\"append an English note at the end\\\",\\n      \\\"keep the behavior behind a small interface\\\",\\n      \\\"make the failure path explicit\\\",\\n      \\\"cache the result to avoid repeating the same expensive operation\\\",\\n      \\\"this change belongs at the module boundary\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"missingPaths\\\": []\\n  },\\n  \\\"cadence\\\": \\\"Force mode bypasses cooldown and daily-cap intent for teachable user prompts; follow the configured note depth and keep the note professional. Skip only when there is no meaningful wording improvement.\\\",\\n  \\\"policy\\\": {\\n    \\\"gateMode\\\": \\\"enforce\\\",\\n    \\\"intensity\\\": \\\"force\\\",\\n    \\\"cooldownMinutes\\\": 0,\\n    \\\"maxInlineCoachingPerDay\\\": 999,\\n    \\\"assistantEnglishNoteDepth\\\": \\\"rich\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"today\\\": {\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-23\\\",\\n    \\\"coachingShown\\\": 0,\\n    \\\"remaining\\\": 999\\n  },\\n  \\\"cooldown\\\": {\\n    \\\"active\\\": false,\\n    \\\"lastShownAt\\\": \\\"2026-08-01T13:52:28.084Z\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"decision\\\": {\\n    \\\"shouldOfferInlineCoaching\\\": true,\\n    \\\"reason\\\": \\\"available\\\"\\n  }\\n}\"}]}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"f33b07\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000012375,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_tok