{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T07:41:32.404Z","ordinal":40466,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1feaf-24d9-7612-a284-664abd64a2c4","turn_id":"01a20756-9c6d-7151-b9aa-d3f86228c963","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-0dac63ab-d1c8-4c89-8917-3585d27664bf","process_id":"70591","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","f=/Users/kingsonwu/.t3/userdata/attachments/9fbeff35-b275-4d28-827e-0793705b1548-3e613045-3824-44c2-9b76-5f5a3edca4d2-md.md; rg -n '^### REQ-002|^### REQ-023|Confirmed scope from user' \"$f\" | head -6; git status --short | rg -i 'call|audio|voice|media|shortcut'; sed -n '843,855p' \"$f\""],"cwd":"file:///Users/kingsonwu/programming/OctopusGarage/mesh-talk","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"f=/Users/kingsonwu/.t3/userdata/attachments/9fbeff35-b275-4d28-827e-0793705b1548-3e613045-3824-44c2-9b76-5f5a3edca4d2-md.md; rg -n '^### REQ-002|^### REQ-023|Confirmed scope from user' \"$f\" | head -6; git status --short | rg -i 'call|audio|voice|media|shortcut'; sed -n '843,855p' \"$f\""}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"75:Discussion states: Captured, Clarifying, Confirmed, Withdrawn, Merged. These describe intake progress, not implementation progress. “Confirmed” means the user explicitly confirmed the stated scope/principle; it never means that technical findings, all details or implementation are approved. “Clarifying” can still contain confirmed sub-decisions. A “Confirmed scope from user” field may summarize the original request rather than a later full-scope sign-off; consult the confirmation wording and audit below.\n144:### REQ-002 — LAN sharing and collaboration tool exploration\n203:- **Confirmed scope from user:** Broad research into mainstream/mature desktop projects; comparison of local versus CI validation and execution placement; diagnosis of Mesh Talk's current workflow; address actual productivity friction rather than deliver generic CI advice.\n241:- **Confirmed scope from user:**\n271:- **Confirmed scope from user:**\n310:- **Confirmed scope from user:** Investigate inefficient full checks/fetches and avoidable writes; consider version comparison to reduce redundant work; organize the write-reduction effort and clarify history-related work. Specific optimization design, deletion policy and acceptance targets are not selected.\n M src-tauri/src/screenshot_shortcuts.rs\n### REQ-023 — LAN real-time voice meetings, with video as a later direction\n\n- **Discussion state:** Clarifying; existing-group initiation and voluntary group-member joining confirmed; scale, controls and protocol dependencies remain open.\n- **Captured / updated:** 2026-11-17 (Asia/Singapore).\n- **Original user input:** “第23个需求：局域网语音实时会议，（以及视频会议后续）这个可能以来群组去中心协议消息同步协议底层先做好，这样才能更好的实现这个功能”。\n- **Scenario and affected users:** People on a LAN participating in a live multiparty voice meeting; video meetings are a later possible expansion.\n- **Pain point or question:** Define how real-time meetings fit the decentralized group and communication model. Existing call/multiparty capabilities and gaps have not been inspected; do not assume no calling support exists.\n- **Desired outcome:** A reliable LAN voice-meeting experience reusing suitable existing foundations, with explicit performance, permissions and lifecycle behavior; video kept as a later direction.\n- **Confirmed scope from user:** Real-time LAN voice meetings now as a requirement topic; video later. User suspects group/decentralized messaging/sync foundations should be improved first; this is a proposed dependency to verify, not a settled development sequence or permission to implement.\n- **Additional confirmed scenario and boundaries:** Start voice meetings from an existing Mesh Talk group; group members actively choose to join. Independent temporary rooms and video remain later directions. Underlying protocol dependencies still require verification. Continue clarification without investigation or implementation.\n- **Additional original user clarification:** “REQ-023 先以现有 Mesh Talk 群聊发起语音会议、群成员主动加入为主要场景；独立临时会议房间和视频保留为后续方向，底层协议依赖仍待验证。请更新文档，继续澄清关键边界，暂不调查或实施。”\n- **Assistant-proposed detailed clarification boundaries — unconfirmed:**\n  - Distinguish meeting admission/invitations, participant/role state and call signaling from real-time audio transport. Reuse identity, permissions and suitable signaling mechanisms without assuming audio should be persisted/replayed as ordinary message history.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":11458}},"started_at_ms":1795419692404,"completed_at_ms":1795419692404}}
