{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T07:41:39.673Z","ordinal":40470,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0dca4931a04d8132016b03ee32087887d09b949f4bb74d9bdb","status":"completed","call_id":"call_c0f254d53eb04911a1b4422c3d017e2e","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:`sed -n '144,173p' /Users/kingsonwu/.t3/userdata/attachments/9fbeff35-b275-4d28-827e-0793705b1548-3e613045-3824-44c2-9b76-5f5a3edca4d2-md.md`}))\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a20756-9c6d-7151-b9aa-d3f86228c963","create_time":1795419698.0383885}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":17156,"sampled_through_sequence":17155,"client_authored":false,"model_search_state":"unused"}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T07:41:39.776Z","ordinal":40471,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1feaf-24d9-7612-a284-664abd64a2c4","turn_id":"01a20756-9c6d-7151-b9aa-d3f86228c963","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-c279a5d1-4b79-4173-aed7-1eb027b5c993","process_id":"79351","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '144,173p' /Users/kingsonwu/.t3/userdata/attachments/9fbeff35-b275-4d28-827e-0793705b1548-3e613045-3824-44c2-9b76-5f5a3edca4d2-md.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/kingsonwu/programming/OctopusGarage/mesh-talk","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '144,173p' /Users/kingsonwu/.t3/userdata/attachments/9fbeff35-b275-4d28-827e-0793705b1548-3e613045-3824-44c2-9b76-5f5a3edca4d2-md.md","name":"9fbeff35-b275-4d28-827e-0793705b1548-3e613045-3824-44c2-9b76-5f5a3edca4d2-md.md","path":"/Users/kingsonwu/.t3/userdata/attachments/9fbeff35-b275-4d28-827e-0793705b1548-3e613045-3824-44c2-9b76-5f5a3edca4d2-md.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"### REQ-002 — LAN sharing and collaboration tool exploration\n\n- **Discussion state:** Clarifying; exploratory idea, not a fixed feature specification.\n- **Captured / updated:** 2026-11-17 (Asia/Singapore).\n- **Original user input:** “第二个需求，应该是功能想法，不一定完全按照以下描述，大概是可以头脑风暴，看看有什么好的局域网工具可以在机遇这个app上开发”。\n- **User-supplied inspiration, not independently verified:** “baoyu-design 增加了局域网内的团队共享功能，现在你的设计稿做好了，或者slides写好了，可以在局域网内分享，生成一个内部 IP 地址加端口的 URL（注意防火墙设置），让你的同事、老板也能对你的内容进行编辑、评论，并且实时同步。安全性也不用担心，所有数据都在你本机，你可以控制分享的权限级别：只读、评论、编辑，并且可以随时修改权限设置。deepseek harness 的插件也同步更新了，一样支持这个功能。” These product claims and the security assurance are supplied inspiration only, not verified facts or adopted guarantees.\n- **Scenario and affected users:** Colleagues on the LAN open shared content in a browser to view it and leave comments without installing Mesh Talk. Designs and slides remain examples; supported formats are not selected.\n- **Pain point or question:** Which LAN collaboration tools would meaningfully complement Mesh Talk? The primary scenario is now confirmed as browser-based viewing and commenting; detailed workflow friction remains to be clarified.\n- **Desired outcome:** Let a Mesh Talk user share content with colleagues who can view and comment through a browser without installing the app. Continue clarifying this review workflow while retaining other LAN collaboration ideas for discussion.\n- **Confirmed conclusions:**\n  - Primary scenario: colleagues need no Mesh Talk installation and use a browser to view and comment on shared content.\n  - Multi-user editing remains a direction for later discussion, outside the currently confirmed primary scenario. Native workspaces and external-tool integrations have not been selected.\n  - The sharer can configure either link-only access or link plus an access code. Per-person approval is not a primary scenario. No default mode has been chosen.\n  - Commenter identity and whether viewing/commenting permissions are separate remain open; do not add an account or per-person approval requirement to the confirmed browser entry flow.\n  - Keep this session in requirements collection and clarification; do not begin development.\n  - Content formats, detailed permission behavior, transport and update semantics remain undecided. The inspiration need not be implemented literally.\n- **Additional original user clarification:** “先以‘同事无需安装 Mesh Talk，通过浏览器查看和评论我分享的内容’为主要场景，多人编辑保留为待讨论方向。请据此更新 REQ-002，继续澄清关键边界，暂不进入开发。”\n- **Additional access clarification from user:** “访问方式先保留为可配置：分享者可选择持有链接即可访问，或链接加访问码；逐人审批暂不作为主要场景。请更新 REQ-002，继续澄清分享内容的类型和评论方式，暂不开发。”\n- **Assistant suggestions / alternatives — unconfirmed, not ranked for global planning:**\n  1. **Share and review existing work:** Publish selected designs, slides, HTML or other supported artifacts into a scoped sharing session; distribute an entry in a conversation and potentially a LAN browser URL. Viewing and comments could address review workflows without requiring an in-app authoring suite. Browser-based viewing and commenting is the confirmed primary direction. Content formats, revisions and entry distribution still require clarification; the detailed solution is not approved.\n  2. **Native collaborative workspace:** Shared notes, whiteboard or lightweight team task board associated with a conversation. Allows direct joint work, but introduces editing semantics, concurrent changes, persistence and recovery responsibilities. These are candidate tools, not promised capabilities.\n  3. **Integration with existing local tools:** Let authorized external tools publish sharing entries or previews through Mesh Talk, keeping authoring in the original tool. Requires deliberate integration, lifecycle and permission boundaries; do not assume an existing API supports this or that Mesh Talk should expose arbitrary local services.\n- **Additional candidate use cases — unconfirmed:** Temporary transfer/download space and team review/decision sessions. Avoid committing to a broad toolbox until real scenarios are clear.\n- **Design considerations to resolve, not fixed requirements:**\n  - Browser participation without installation and sharer-configurable link-only/link-plus-code entry are confirmed. A reachable IP/port alone is not the scoped sharing link; exact link scope and access-code behavior remain to be designed.\n  - In link-only mode forwarding the sharing link can pass access onward; in access-code mode the link and code can both be forwarded. Per-person approval is outside the primary scenario. Expiry, code changes, revocation and view/comment permissions still need decisions; no default mode selected.\n  - Comment identity may be a self-entered nickname or verified identity; do not imply a nickname proves who submitted a comment. Comment persistence, replies, deletion/moderation and attachment to a page/region/version remain open.\n  - Decide which content is shared and how safely it can be presented. An immutable published snapshot and a live local-file view have different update and comment-anchoring behavior. Do not assume arbitrary HTML can run with host/app privileges or that sharing one item exposes a directory.\n  - Local storage alone does not establish confidentiality or safe access. Distinguish host storage, recipient/browser copies, authentication, transport protection and enforced read/comment/edit permissions.\n  - Specify permission changes and revocation for already-open sessions; stopping future access cannot recall copies already downloaded. Avoid inheriting the quoted unconditional security assurance.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":10833}},"started_at_ms":1795419699776,"completed_at_ms":1795419699776}}
