{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T07:52:30.743Z","ordinal":40811,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1feaf-24d9-7612-a284-664abd64a2c4","turn_id":"01a20762-5c03-7890-9803-b4777050947a","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-ec395b9c-83a3-4fa7-9cf9-20bda49ef9c7","process_id":"14383","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n -i 'unchanged.*projection|maintenance.*authorization|receive.key|account-channel' docs/network-design-reference.md | tail -20; rg -n -i 'mainten|bounded.*key' crates/mesh-talk-core/validation.json | rg 'group|channel' | head -20; tail -8 tmp/req-011/quiet-account-group-green.log"],"cwd":"file:///Users/kingsonwu/programming/OctopusGarage/mesh-talk","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rg -n -i 'unchanged.*projection|maintenance.*authorization|receive.key|account-channel' docs/network-design-reference.md | tail -20; rg -n -i 'mainten|bounded.*key' crates/mesh-talk-core/validation.json | rg 'group|channel' | head -20; tail -8 tmp/req-011/quiet-account-group-green.log"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"1242:input remain unchanged: group/identity/privacy projection, sharing pause state,\n2017:an unchanged own projection without repeating its signature checks under the\n3939:Account-channel and custody schedulers observe this storage-backed hint through\n30:        \"crates/mesh-talk-core/src/node/channel_account_maintenance.rs\",\n171:            \"name\": \"Account-maintenance peer waits cannot block bounded local channel preparation or mandatory Directory publication; one parent owns local recovery, account maintenance and custody futures, independent wake subscriptions preserve local demand, and cancellation joins the complete lifetime. The existing serial three-second custody turn progresses during unrelated history/fallback waits; that custody turn adds no task or transport allowance. Selected public peer exchanges retain separately owned bounded children under the participant retirement barrier.\",\n247:            \"name\": \"Authenticated body-free sibling invalidations remain active when all optional history, attachment, appearance and contact categories are disabled; mandatory group control latency does not depend on the periodic repair tick, a held mandatory directory response, or unrelated local maintenance outside shared storage guards. One admitted local storage turn runs independently of document dispatch, coalesces real changes without a completion-driven loop, and retains actual-work retirement. Attachment selection rechecks current reservations on handoff and preserves durable rotating scans; failed exact-source fanout refresh defers its original revision. Ordinary and legacy operation publishers serialize each projection and signed merge through their feature-owned per-Node unit gate, including invitation completion; no publication gate spans network work. Control, directory, optional document and history/favorites work retain independent cursors and one reserved worker each within the existing four-worker and shared TCP budgets; optional document progress preserves its category and entitlement checks independently of held archive responses.\",\n331:            \"node::channel_account_maintenance::tests::scheduling_input_waits_for_history_without_blocking_its_reactor\",\n384:        \"Require real legacy-owner/member/sibling private-session convergence, source-offline restart, adoption scoping, policy-off metadata-only transfer, bounded roster and no-authority assertions. In mandatory-wake acceptance, retain the first signed source floor and first receiver-head times plus bounded actual inventory Header/Complete evidence; negative coverage first establishes actual Owner access and an equal signed inventory baseline inside the existing cold setup watchdog, then holds a strictly newer exact-source header outside storage locks until the original five-second cutoff. Capture the baseline validated signed GroupControl Owner grant and independently require a current signed Owner grant for the same group/source/account and physical owner binding at that cutoff. Normal same-account auto-enrollment and authority migration may choose a different physical membership representative; do not require cross-baseline MembershipLifetime equality. Independently validate the actual current Owner grant after ordinary canonical-generation/epoch/representative changes. Permit only explicit transient StaleCursor or Unknown/Reconciling alongside that retained evidence; reject unexpected errors, changed/terminal roles, unavailable and unrelated signed heads. Exercise held_inventory_owner_evidence_rejects_signed_terminal_unavailable_and_unrelated_heads and keep diagnostics to safe role/execution/error classes. Require the first fresh signed floor and changed member label, exact held-header version, live hook task, retained old receiver baseline and absent fresh inventory; keep the positive creation window unchanged. Qualify a bounded registry of actual live server-header holders for the exact peer/account/key/writer at or above the immutable first fresh source floor, with the gate armed. A retired last request or a signed superseding head must not erase another qualifying live holder; stale, wrong-scope, released, empty and overflowed registries fail. Exercise held_inventory_headers_preserve_live_overlaps_and_reject_unqualified_holds without changing either five-second window. Hold an unrelated authenticated group sync response before appending a new local group, then require multiple bounded local turns, signed source Directory publication and exact sibling import within the original eight-second watchdog while that response remains held. Force one real authenticated setup exchange to fail before the hold, then snapshot exact-peer/group begin and end counters at actual hold entry. Require one live round, unchanged counters and live transport throughout publication; earlier setup failures must not invalidate the measured window, and timeout, completion or replacement must not rescue it. Test transactional completion handoff with two queued identities, repeated nonqueued completion and an empty queue. Preserve network target wakes, quiet deduplication, retry backoff, custody denial and parent-owned cancellation. Reference state must never enter authoritative group or peer binding stores.\",\n939:        \"crates/mesh-talk-core/src/node/channel_account_maintenance.rs\",\n959:            \"node::channel_account_maintenance::tests::\",\n991:            \"node::channel_account_maintenance::tests::\",\n1036:            \"name\": \"Capability maintenance probes only sibling or existing group relationships and never competes with an unrelated discovered DM route. Ordinary unchanged wakes respect retained retry deadlines even for incomplete cycles; scheduling observation never acknowledges success, while fresh semantics, failed observations, explicit drivers and timer-disabled recovery remain live.\",\n   Compiling mesh-talk-core v0.4.6 (/Users/kingsonwu/programming/OctopusGarage/mesh-talk/crates/mesh-talk-core)\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":11833}},"started_at_ms":1795420350743,"completed_at_ms":1795420350743}}
