ed heads. Exercise held_inventory_owner_evidence_rejects_signed_terminal_unavailable_and_unrelated_heads and keep diagnostics to safe role/execution/error classes. Require the first fresh signed floor and changed member label, exact held-header version, live hook task, retained old receiver baseline and absent fresh inventory; keep the positive creation window unchanged. Qualify a bounded registry of actual live server-header holders for the exact peer/account/key/writer at or above the immutable first fresh source floor, with the gate armed. A retired last request or a signed superseding head must not erase another qualifying live holder; stale, wrong-scope, released, empty and overflowed registries fail. Exercise held_inventory_headers_preserve_live_overlaps_and_reject_unqualified_holds without changing either five-second window. Hold an unrelated authenticated group sync response before appending a new local group, then require multiple bounded local turns, signed source Directory publication and exact sibling import within the original eight-second watchdog while that response remains held. Force one real authenticated setup exchange to fail before the hold, then snapshot exact-peer/group begin and end counters at actual hold entry. Require one live round, unchanged counters and live transport throughout publication; earlier setup failures must not invalidate the measured window, and timeout, completion or replacement must not rescue it. Test transactional completion handoff with two queued identities, repeated nonqueued completion and an empty queue. Preserve network target wakes, quiet deduplication, retry backoff, custody denial and parent-owned cancellation. Reference state must never enter authoritative group or peer binding stores.\\\",\\n939:        \\\"crates/mesh-talk-core/src/node/channel_account_maintenance.rs\\\",\\n959:            \\\"node::channel_account_maintenance::tests::\\\",\\n991:            \\\"node::channel_account_maintenance::tests::\\\",\\n1036:            \\\"name\\\": \\\"Capability maintenance probes only sibling or existing group relationships and never competes with an unrelated discovered DM route. Ordinary unchanged wakes respect retained retry deadlines even for incomplete cycles; scheduling observation never acknowledges success, while fresh semantics, failed observations, explicit drivers and timer-disabled recovery remain live.\\\",\\n   Compiling mesh-talk-core v0.4.6 (/Users/kingsonwu/programming/OctopusGarage/mesh-talk/crates/mesh-talk-core)\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a20762-5c03-7890-9803-b4777050947a","create_time":1795420350.932439}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":17295,"sampled_through_sequence":17292,"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000,"model_search_state":"unused"}}
