{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T07:52:39.051Z","ordinal":40817,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0dca4931a04d8132016b03f0c5fed887d0bfcf2f446f640bc8","status":"completed","call_id":"call_71c4aecf953448e3829b66cd042b136d","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:`sed -n '3926,3955p' docs/network-design-reference.md; sed -n '1029,1043p' crates/mesh-talk-core/validation.json; tail -5 tmp/req-011/quiet-account-group-green.log`}))\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a20762-5c03-7890-9803-b4777050947a","create_time":1795420357.9999208}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":17297,"sampled_through_sequence":17295,"client_authored":false,"model_search_state":"unused"}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T07:52:39.219Z","ordinal":40818,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1feaf-24d9-7612-a284-664abd64a2c4","turn_id":"01a20762-5c03-7890-9803-b4777050947a","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-4e49538b-f02d-41af-b35a-999c5dfc5ea0","process_id":"8746","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '3926,3955p' docs/network-design-reference.md; sed -n '1029,1043p' crates/mesh-talk-core/validation.json; tail -5 tmp/req-011/quiet-account-group-green.log"],"cwd":"file:///Users/kingsonwu/programming/OctopusGarage/mesh-talk","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"sed -n '3926,3955p' docs/network-design-reference.md; sed -n '1029,1043p' crates/mesh-talk-core/validation.json; tail -5 tmp/req-011/quiet-account-group-green.log"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"local committed mutations wake publication immediately.\n\nRoutine local group-access/inventory publication compares the existing source,\nprofile, proof, policy, document and device metadata before reading bodies.\nRoster and registered-device owners each retain one lazy 32-byte content digest\nunder their existing lock. Roster identity includes all exported filtered historical\nand live signed announcements; registered-device identity includes its account and\ncomplete canonical devices. Successful content mutations invalidate these hints;\nunchanged heartbeats and duplicate device records do not rebuild them. Device\npersistence failure cannot publish a new digest. The domain-separated outer\nprojection hint still captures current source, privacy, policy, profile, proof,\ndocument and group inputs. Digest reuse grants no permission, extends no presence\nlease and suppresses no route or expiry observation.\nAccount-channel and custody schedulers observe this storage-backed hint through\nthe existing single local-repair slot. The actual blocking worker owns its slot\nand retirement admission through cancellation; observation returns only after\nreleasing them, before any network exchange. The synchronous projection remains\navailable to existing storage workers and direct readers.\nThe lifetime-owned maintenance cursor retains its pre-work input across bounded\npages; newer inputs retain a follow-up. Failed publication stays dirty with its\nown five-second retry deadline; a settled pass keeps a five-minute integrity\nrepair deadline. Those timers wake local work without manufacturing peer refresh\ntraffic. Direct document reads and authorization retain their integrity checks.\n\nFederation wakes on durable mailbox, directory and effective route changes,\ncoalesces bursts and caches unchanged inventories. Consecutive full mailbox\nbatches continue with a per-edge delay growing from 100 milliseconds to at most\nfive seconds, so inconsistent inventories or retention churn cannot create\nunbounded immediate reconciliation. A drained batch resets that delay. Mail and\npresence notifications do not bypass a saturated edge's continuation deadline;\n            \"reference\": \"docs/help/topics/channels.md#review-membership\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"name\": \"Account revocations merge without resurrection, reinvitation requires fresh consent, and independent sender chains exclude consumed historical keys\",\n            \"reference\": \"docs/network-design-reference.md#d-group-creation-distribution-and-member-recovery\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"name\": \"Capability maintenance probes only sibling or existing group relationships and never competes with an unrelated discovered DM route. Ordinary unchanged wakes respect retained retry deadlines even for incomplete cycles; scheduling observation never acknowledges success, while fresh semantics, failed observations, explicit drivers and timer-disabled recovery remain live.\",\n            \"reference\": \"docs/network-design-reference.md#d-group-creation-distribution-and-member-recovery\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"name\": \"Compatible legacy migration requires established verified bindings and bounded capability checks; V4 sync protects older envelopes from new control kinds\",\n            \"reference\": \"docs/network-design-reference.md#d-group-creation-distribution-and-member-recovery\"\n          },\n          {\n   Compiling mesh-talk-core v0.4.6 (/Users/kingsonwu/programming/OctopusGarage/mesh-talk/crates/mesh-talk-core)\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":21208}},"started_at_ms":1795420359218,"completed_at_ms":1795420359219}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T07:52:39.872Z","ordinal":40819,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a1feaf-24d9-7612-a284-664abd64a2c4","turn_id":"01a20762-5c03-7890-9803-b4777050947a","session_id":"01a1feaf-24d9-7612-a284-664abd64a2c4","root_turn_id":"01a20762-5c03-7890-9803-b4777050947a","response_id":"resp_0dca4931a04d8132016b03f0c1b3c087d0b1c0bd383486a2d9","usage":{"input_tokens":439205,"cached_input_tokens":437888,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":106,"reasoning_output_tokens":33,"total_tokens":439311},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":3920821,"cached_input_tokens":3913344,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1094,"reasoning_output_tokens":318,"total_tokens":3921915},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":1481502034,"cached_input_tokens":1475538944,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1275917,"reasoning_output_tokens":329376,"total_tokens":1482777951}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-23T07:52:39.884Z","ordinal":40820,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a20764-8ccc-77d2-9365-7513978c3368","call_id":"call_71c4aecf953448e3829b66cd042b136d","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.3 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"338cc3\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000021208,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":878,\"output\":\"local committed mutations wake publication immediately.\\n\\nRoutine local group-access/inventory publication compares the existing source,\\nprofile, proof, policy, document and device metadata before reading bodies.\\nRoster and registered-device owners each retain one lazy 32-byte content digest\\nunder their existing lock. Roster identity includes all exported filtered historical\\nand live signed announcements; registered-device identity includes its account and\\ncomplete canonical devices. Successful content mutations invalidate these hints;\\nunchanged heartbeats and duplicate device records do not rebuild them. Device\\npersistence failure cannot publish a new digest. The domain-separated outer\\nprojection hint still captures current source, privacy, policy, profile, proof,\\ndocument and group inputs. Digest reuse grants no permission, extends no presence\\nlease and suppresses no route or expiry observation.\\nAccount-channel and custody schedulers observe this storage-backed hint through\\nthe existing single local-repair slot. The actual blocking worker owns its slot\\nand retirement admission through cancellation; observation returns only after\\nreleasing them, before any network exchange. The synchronous projection remains\\navailable to existing storage workers and direct readers.\\nThe lifetime-owned maintenance cursor retains its pre-work input across bounded\\npages; newer inputs retain a follow-up. Failed publication stays dirty with its\\nown five-second retry deadline; a settled pass keeps a five-minute integrity\\nrepair deadline. Those timers wake local work without manufacturing peer refresh\\ntraffic. Direct document reads and authorization retain their integrity checks.\\n\\nFederation wakes on durable mailbox, directory and effective route changes,\\ncoalesces bursts and caches unchanged inventories. Consecutive full mailbox\\nbatches continue with a per-edge delay growing from 100 milliseconds to at most\\nfive seconds, so inconsistent inventories or retention churn cannot create\\nunbounded immediate reconciliation. A drained batch resets that delay. Mail and\\npresence notifications do not bypass a saturated edge's continuation deadline;\\n            \\\"reference\\\": \\\"docs/help/topics/channels.md#review-membership\\\"\\n          },\\n          {\\n            \\\"name\\\": \\\"Account revocations merge without resurrection, reinvitation requires fresh consent, and independent sender chains exclude consumed historical keys\\\",\\n            \\\"reference\\\": \\\"docs/network-design-reference.md#d-group-creation-distribution-and-member-recovery\\\"\\n          },\\n          {\\n            \\\"name\\\": \\\"Capability maintenance probes only sibling or existing group relationships and never competes with an unrelated discovered DM route. Ordinary unchanged wakes respect retained retry deadlines even for incomplete cycles; scheduling observation never acknowledges success, while fresh semantics, failed observations, explicit drivers and timer-disabled recovery remain live.\\\",\\n            \\\"reference\\\": \\\"docs/network-design-reference.md#d-group-creation-distribution-and-member-recovery\\\"\\n          },\\n          {\\n            \\\"name\\\": \\\"Compatible legacy migration requires established verified bindings and bounded capability checks; V4 sync protects older envelopes from new control kinds\\\",\\n            \\\"reference\\\": \\\"docs/network-design-reference.md#d-group-creation-distribution-and-member-recovery\\\"